1
00:00:00,711 --> 00:00:05,311
[As Luxor’s deep night fades away,]

2
00:00:06,645 --> 00:00:11,178
[the morning arrives with birdsong]

3
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:14,745
[The paupers are
still sound asleep]

4
00:00:15,478 --> 00:00:19,211
[Rustle]

5
00:00:19,501 --> 00:00:21,278
Wow…

6
00:00:21,279 --> 00:00:22,678
It's so hot.

7
00:00:24,111 --> 00:00:25,378
[Bolts up]

8
00:00:25,379 --> 00:00:26,278
Ugh…

9
00:00:27,111 --> 00:00:30,478
[The paupers wake up
due to sunshine issues]

10
00:00:31,511 --> 00:00:32,145
Wow!

11
00:00:32,878 --> 00:00:34,811
Wow! Look at the sky! Wow!!

12
00:00:36,045 --> 00:00:37,478
What the...!

13
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:39,680
[The morning sunlight peeks through the clouds]
Hey, the sky totally changed!

14
00:00:39,681 --> 00:00:41,378
Wow, this is amazing.

15
00:00:42,411 --> 00:00:44,345
SHINDONG, do you know
how horses cry?

16
00:00:44,346 --> 00:00:45,845
Horses come here?

17
00:00:46,311 --> 00:00:47,911
The horses cry…

18
00:00:47,912 --> 00:00:49,078
How do horses cry?

19
00:00:49,079 --> 00:00:50,645
Uh-huh… Uh-huh…
They cry like this.

20
00:00:51,381 --> 00:00:52,378
Stop lying.

21
00:00:52,378 --> 00:00:53,159
[Focused on being funny
first thing in the morning]

22
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,783
- I'm serious!
- No, you've gone too far.

23
00:00:54,783 --> 00:00:56,311
I actually woke up
because of that, for real.

24
00:00:56,312 --> 00:00:58,977
Hey…It's not like
horses are pop stars or anything.

25
00:00:58,978 --> 00:01:00,511
YOHAN must've dreamed it.

26
00:01:00,512 --> 00:01:01,311
Seriously!

27
00:01:01,312 --> 00:01:02,278
[Unfair]
So, how do horses cry?

28
00:01:02,279 --> 00:01:03,381
Uh-huh, uh-huh, like this!

29
00:01:03,382 --> 00:01:04,867
- What is that?
- I'm serious!

30
00:01:04,868 --> 00:01:06,196
[A debate about horses and pop stars starts their morning]
Come on, don't lie.

31
00:01:06,197 --> 00:01:07,579
(Grumbling)
Wow, this place has all sorts of animals…

32
00:01:07,579 --> 00:01:09,078
Oh, this is so refreshing!

33
00:01:09,079 --> 00:01:10,945
The weather's insane! Wow!

34
00:01:11,184 --> 00:01:12,678
[Not caring about the horse]
Wait, what now all of a sudden?

35
00:01:12,679 --> 00:01:16,078
[Completely soaking in the morning vibes]
Whoa!

36
00:01:16,079 --> 00:01:16,978
Wow, no way!

37
00:01:16,979 --> 00:01:19,978
[A movie-like morning scene]
This is so nice!

38
00:01:20,745 --> 00:01:23,778
Like, why were they whining
so much over something like this?

39
00:01:23,779 --> 00:01:25,445
[Whiny pauper]

40
00:01:25,446 --> 00:01:26,577
[So unfair]
This is so nice!

41
00:01:26,578 --> 00:01:28,685
this is seriously
royal treatment.

42
00:01:28,686 --> 00:01:30,178
(Yesterday)
compared to yesterday…

43
00:01:30,179 --> 00:01:32,378
If we put Day 1
and Day 2 side by side,

44
00:01:32,379 --> 00:01:34,811
there's like
a night and day difference

45
00:01:35,445 --> 00:01:37,278
For Day 1…

46
00:01:37,911 --> 00:01:39,778
Ha…

47
00:01:39,779 --> 00:01:41,711
If it felt like eating dirt,

48
00:01:41,712 --> 00:01:44,945
Day 2 was like
eating rice and kimchi…

49
00:01:44,946 --> 00:01:46,571
[A satisfied review of the pauper accommodation: ★★★★★]
The sleeping bags were nice.

50
00:01:46,572 --> 00:01:48,745
I crashed the moment I went in.

51
00:01:49,078 --> 00:01:53,311
[Meanwhile, the morning arrives
on the Nile River cruise too]

52
00:01:54,445 --> 00:01:57,511
[Wonder what our princes are up to?]

53
00:01:59,576 --> 00:02:01,678
[Prince / Selfie / My chill morning]
Time was moving slower than I thought,

54
00:02:01,679 --> 00:02:03,411
and it felt like
such a waste to sleep…

55
00:02:03,778 --> 00:02:05,345
I just feel at ease.

56
00:02:06,678 --> 00:02:09,778
I think I vibe well with Egypt.

57
00:02:10,045 --> 00:02:11,945
[Utopia]

58
00:02:12,238 --> 00:02:15,371
[Could this be heaven...?]
I came to heaven and opened the door,

59
00:02:15,379 --> 00:02:17,078
[Sunshine and clouds say hello here]
and with the sunshine pouring in,

60
00:02:17,079 --> 00:02:19,178
it felt like the clouds were hugging me.

61
00:02:19,611 --> 00:02:21,178
[So satisfied with the prince life]
I was so happy.

62
00:02:21,179 --> 00:02:23,578
The breeze was
giving me a massage.

63
00:02:26,062 --> 00:02:27,084
Friend, friend!

64
00:02:27,092 --> 00:02:28,871
[Time to interrupt their peaceful morning]

65
00:02:28,872 --> 00:02:30,078
My friend, my bro!

66
00:02:30,611 --> 00:02:33,311
[Dressed in mysterious clothes,]

67
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:36,411
[the paupers board the prince's ship]
Korea.

68
00:02:37,111 --> 00:02:39,278
Assalamu alaikum!

69
00:02:39,811 --> 00:02:42,445
[The paupers are BACK]

70
00:02:43,055 --> 00:02:46,278
[Why did these guys show up like this?]
My friend, my friend!

71
00:02:46,445 --> 00:02:47,256
[Last night]

72
00:02:47,257 --> 00:02:48,911
I'm the prince!

73
00:02:49,345 --> 00:02:52,078
[After the princes left…]
I must be royalty!

74
00:02:52,079 --> 00:02:53,111
I can't believe this.

75
00:02:53,112 --> 00:02:55,278
Our three paupers now…

76
00:02:56,378 --> 00:02:58,011
Today,

77
00:02:58,012 --> 00:02:59,145
for all of you,

78
00:03:00,445 --> 00:03:02,478
- we prepared…
- Oh!

79
00:03:02,479 --> 00:03:04,278
- A life-changing opportunity.
- Oh!

80
00:03:05,011 --> 00:03:07,211
[Dopamine recharge]
What’s that? What could it be?

81
00:03:07,212 --> 00:03:09,911
Become the merchants
of the Nile River,

82
00:03:10,838 --> 00:03:13,804
[After buying items at the market,]
and go shopping with the money we give you.

83
00:03:13,825 --> 00:03:15,411
[sell to the princes]
Tomorrow, if you sell what you bought to the princes

84
00:03:15,412 --> 00:03:17,991
[at a high price tomorrow!]
at a high price, you'll receive a perk!

85
00:03:18,711 --> 00:03:20,845
[The pauper with the
biggest profit gets a special reward]

86
00:03:20,846 --> 00:03:22,248
When you visit Egypt,

87
00:03:22,249 --> 00:03:24,578
[The golden rule of Egyptian shopping = Bargaining]
it's said to be a country where bargaining is part of the fun.

88
00:03:25,011 --> 00:03:26,578
[Depending on how I bargain,]
Discount?

89
00:03:26,579 --> 00:03:28,975
[my profit margin will change!]
Please, please!

90
00:03:28,976 --> 00:03:31,678
[With 3,000 EGP each, they head to the market!]
Everyone will each get 3,000 Egyptian pounds.

91
00:03:31,679 --> 00:03:33,078
[= About 90,000 won]
That’s roughly 90,000 won in Korean currency.

92
00:03:33,079 --> 00:03:34,411
- Wow!
- Wow!

93
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:37,482
Then, let's begin!

94
00:03:37,483 --> 00:03:39,470
[Self-Cams ON
in Luxor Market]

95
00:03:40,245 --> 00:03:42,778
[Full of curiosity]
Alright, it's very…

96
00:03:43,068 --> 00:03:45,445
But it’s not the market I imagined!

97
00:03:46,078 --> 00:03:48,145
The deeper we go,
the cooler it gets.

98
00:03:49,178 --> 00:03:51,611
[They must buy something here
to sell to the princes]

99
00:03:51,612 --> 00:03:54,245
(At the lowest price possible)

100
00:03:57,445 --> 00:03:58,978
[Spotted something]
Oh!

101
00:03:59,081 --> 00:04:02,511
"There's no store
as nice and fun as this place…"

102
00:04:03,445 --> 00:04:05,178
"Kind Eid and Ahmed…"

103
00:04:05,179 --> 00:04:07,245
[Traces of Koreans found in Egypt]
Oho!

104
00:04:08,111 --> 00:04:11,278
[Entering as if under a trance]
Oh! Mr. Ahmed!

105
00:04:12,378 --> 00:04:14,111
I like Korea!

106
00:04:14,275 --> 00:04:16,781
It says he's stubborn
when it comes to bargaining prices.

107
00:04:17,749 --> 00:04:20,478
When I first went through the market,
I went into a store,

108
00:04:20,678 --> 00:04:23,178
and a lot of
Korean people visited that store.

109
00:04:23,179 --> 00:04:25,378
And what they wrote
as reviews was…

110
00:04:25,568 --> 00:04:28,097
"This man is super stubborn,
so bargain until the end."

111
00:04:28,111 --> 00:04:28,979
That’s exactly what it said.

112
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:30,478
[Okay! This is how you do it!]
Okay! This is it!

113
00:04:34,345 --> 00:04:37,011
(Spotted something)

114
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:38,978
(This one?)

115
00:04:38,979 --> 00:04:39,778
Oh, yes!

116
00:04:39,779 --> 00:04:43,245
[Found some papyrus souvenirs]
Oh, good! Okay!

117
00:04:44,056 --> 00:04:44,910
Nice.

118
00:04:44,911 --> 00:04:47,145
[Quick purchase decision]
I think I can sell this easily.

119
00:04:47,611 --> 00:04:49,611
(As cheap as possible!)
[First round of bargaining]

120
00:04:50,245 --> 00:04:52,212
[Bargaining Battle, START]
[Ahmed vs SHINDONG]

121
00:04:52,845 --> 00:04:54,645
(The first offer)

122
00:04:55,178 --> 00:04:56,578
350 EGP each for 3 pieces,
so a total of 1,050 EGP.

123
00:04:56,579 --> 00:04:59,945
[About 30,000 KRW]
Ohhhhh…

124
00:05:00,245 --> 00:05:01,278
(So this is how it goes)
Nooooo…

125
00:05:01,279 --> 00:05:03,011
Okay, tell me the price you want.

126
00:05:03,878 --> 00:05:04,978
[Testing the waters]

127
00:05:04,979 --> 00:05:06,545
Make you happy, I'm happy.

128
00:05:06,546 --> 00:05:08,411
[1,050]
[300]

129
00:05:08,411 --> 00:05:11,383
I’m happy!

130
00:05:11,384 --> 00:05:12,517
Not happy!

131
00:05:12,576 --> 00:05:14,745
Very happy!

132
00:05:14,978 --> 00:05:16,945
[-70%]
I'm not happy!

133
00:05:16,946 --> 00:05:18,679
Okay, last!

134
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,078
[300]
[500]

135
00:05:20,079 --> 00:05:21,378
[Ugh...]

136
00:05:22,145 --> 00:05:23,645
[Fed up]
Okay!

137
00:05:23,646 --> 00:05:26,011
[This Korean is not so easy]

138
00:05:26,645 --> 00:05:28,678
You said 500 EGP.

139
00:05:28,945 --> 00:05:31,045
[Let’s find a way to make us both happy]
Between happy, I'm happy!

140
00:05:31,511 --> 00:05:33,545
[This is our happy price]

141
00:05:34,378 --> 00:05:35,978
Smile, happy!
I'm happy!

142
00:05:35,979 --> 00:05:37,378
So, just smile.

143
00:05:37,379 --> 00:05:40,578
I’m not happy...

144
00:05:40,911 --> 00:05:41,811
[Playing the pity card]
Please...

145
00:05:41,812 --> 00:05:44,478
[Me too, please]

146
00:05:44,778 --> 00:05:46,111
I'm not talking anymore!

147
00:05:46,112 --> 00:05:48,245
- I’m not talking anymore.
- Okay.

148
00:05:48,246 --> 00:05:49,661
[Really fed up]
This is my final offer.

149
00:05:49,662 --> 00:05:50,378
Okay.

150
00:05:52,145 --> 00:05:54,545
[Lowered it a lot...]
Now say you like it...!

151
00:05:55,278 --> 00:05:55,811
Okay, last...

152
00:05:55,819 --> 00:05:57,361
No!!! No more talking!!!!!

153
00:05:57,362 --> 00:05:58,243
Last!

154
00:05:58,245 --> 00:05:59,945
[Unfazed]
Last!

155
00:05:59,946 --> 00:06:01,180
Last, okay?

156
00:06:01,181 --> 00:06:03,071
[I lost...]
Okay.

157
00:06:03,678 --> 00:06:05,569
[Successfully reconciled]
Good!

158
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:07,078
I got it!
Okay!

159
00:06:07,311 --> 00:06:08,978
I think it's still really expensive…

160
00:06:08,979 --> 00:06:11,278
[He was a tough one]
You very hard! Very, very hard.

161
00:06:11,811 --> 00:06:12,945
Thank you.

162
00:06:12,946 --> 00:06:14,145
Good friend!

163
00:06:14,146 --> 00:06:15,345
You happy?

164
00:06:16,411 --> 00:06:19,144
[Friend, are you happy?]
You happy? I like you, Korea!

165
00:06:19,145 --> 00:06:21,278
[Purchased one item for now]
Together, happy.

166
00:06:22,778 --> 00:06:23,778
[WOW]
Wow!

167
00:06:25,388 --> 00:06:26,588
[The sphinx spotted]
Hey, this is the sphinx!

168
00:06:26,589 --> 00:06:28,211
Oh, these are all sphinxes here.

169
00:06:28,212 --> 00:06:29,711
[Pharaoh spotted]
There are even pharaohs here, too.

170
00:06:30,790 --> 00:06:31,883
Oh, over there…!

171
00:06:33,363 --> 00:06:36,190
[Found something cute]
This is seriously adorable, like super cute!

172
00:06:36,191 --> 00:06:40,111
[Found something pretty]
This one’s really pretty too, though!

173
00:06:40,645 --> 00:06:43,178
[Just browsing
all day without buying…]

174
00:06:44,163 --> 00:06:46,784
I mean, stuff like this
definitely seems very Egyptian.

175
00:06:46,785 --> 00:06:48,879
If you wear this in a fight,
it would really hurt.

176
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:51,683
[Self-defense item found]
It has such sharp edges! Wow, this…

177
00:06:51,684 --> 00:06:55,278
[Found something noisy and cool]
This makes noise and is cool

178
00:06:56,668 --> 00:07:00,145
[You’re not gonna buy it...?]
I really like things like this, this kind of thing.

179
00:07:00,745 --> 00:07:02,978
What should I buy?

180
00:07:03,189 --> 00:07:05,178
[At least this guy knows what he should be doing]
Like…

181
00:07:05,179 --> 00:07:09,045
[Merchant YOHAN’s strategy: Exclusive and high-quality]
Something that looks a bit fancy.

182
00:07:09,256 --> 00:07:10,445
Oh!

183
00:07:10,770 --> 00:07:13,811
[A traditional outfit spotted]
I’m really drawn to this one.

184
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:16,579
[Strategy #2]
Because, honestly,

185
00:07:16,587 --> 00:07:19,111
[Offering a unique experience]
you don't really get a chance to wear something like this!

186
00:07:19,985 --> 00:07:22,085
Let's keep moving for now.
I'll save this place for the time being.

187
00:07:22,584 --> 00:07:23,591
I'm saving this place!

188
00:07:24,870 --> 00:07:26,676
They really carve this, right?
How much is this?

189
00:07:26,677 --> 00:07:29,278
[Stopped in front of
a stone engraving shop]

190
00:07:31,068 --> 00:07:32,278
I wanna get something cool...

191
00:07:32,279 --> 00:07:33,811
(You don’t like it?)

192
00:07:34,073 --> 00:07:36,093
Something…lucky.

193
00:07:36,094 --> 00:07:38,545
[Paraphrasing:
I'd like something that means good luck]

194
00:07:38,845 --> 00:07:40,045
I'll carve your name
on the stone slab

195
00:07:40,046 --> 00:07:43,412
and make it
so you can hang it on the wall.

196
00:07:43,578 --> 00:07:44,778
Handmake?

197
00:07:44,779 --> 00:07:46,645
Me, I make it by my hand!

198
00:07:46,646 --> 00:07:49,445
The shop owner
at the market intersection

199
00:07:49,446 --> 00:07:52,511
was carving
the stone slabs by hand.

200
00:07:52,512 --> 00:07:53,875
[His kind of vibe]
And on top of that,

201
00:07:53,876 --> 00:07:56,378
[He even offers a custom engraving]
he engraves whatever you want.

202
00:07:56,578 --> 00:07:58,311
[Perfect for his exclusive & high-quality strategy]
I need to buy this.

203
00:07:58,312 --> 00:08:00,211
This would be meaningful.

204
00:08:01,611 --> 00:08:03,062
[I’ll carve it right here]
What’s your name?

205
00:08:03,063 --> 00:08:04,611
Oh, what's your name!

206
00:08:04,612 --> 00:08:07,411
[Gotta engrave the buyer’s name]
But I can't engrave my name on this!

207
00:08:09,372 --> 00:08:11,011
[Target buyer: LEETEUK]
Let's go with LEETEUK!

208
00:08:11,367 --> 00:08:12,278
Oh, LEE…LEE…

209
00:08:12,279 --> 00:08:15,078
(How do I spell LEETEUK in English…)
[Help me]

210
00:08:16,678 --> 00:08:19,611
[Real name PARK JUNG SOO - Decided on JS]
JS. JS.

211
00:08:20,245 --> 00:08:21,264
(Working hard…)
J…

212
00:08:21,265 --> 00:08:22,678
S.

213
00:08:23,611 --> 00:08:25,083
[Planning on selling it to LEETEUK]
Okay, lucky!

214
00:08:25,084 --> 00:08:27,011
[JS]
Thank you, thank you!

215
00:08:28,211 --> 00:08:30,811
Thank you!
Bye-bye!

216
00:08:31,478 --> 00:08:33,175
[While YOHAN was
making a quick purchase...]

217
00:08:33,176 --> 00:08:34,145
It is pretty cool.

218
00:08:35,445 --> 00:08:38,478
This place is…
Wow, seriously…

219
00:08:38,479 --> 00:08:40,545
(INFP/J)
A world meant for extroverts…

220
00:08:40,784 --> 00:08:43,784
[Not even buying, but his energy is getting drained]
An introvert who fell into the world of extroverts…

221
00:08:44,778 --> 00:08:47,211
[Another super
extroverted vendor appears]

222
00:08:47,212 --> 00:08:48,811
Oh wow, it’s... amazing...

223
00:08:49,211 --> 00:08:51,045
[Listen to me]
I made it all by hand!

224
00:08:51,046 --> 00:08:53,211
Handmade...!
Wow, oh my god...

225
00:08:53,468 --> 00:08:56,145
[You've got an impressive skill…!]
So good hand skill.

226
00:08:57,078 --> 00:09:00,811
[YOHAN approaches JISUNG]
I’ve still got some money left.

227
00:09:00,812 --> 00:09:02,578
[Spotted an alcohol shop]
Should we buy some beer with this?

228
00:09:02,579 --> 00:09:04,178
[Tempted]
That would be really nice.

229
00:09:04,911 --> 00:09:07,280
[Egypt Trip]
It was here! Look at this!

230
00:09:07,281 --> 00:09:09,078
[In Egypt, with its Islamic culture,]
This is amazing.

231
00:09:09,079 --> 00:09:11,111
[alcohol can only be bought
at designated liquor stores & hotels]

232
00:09:11,112 --> 00:09:13,345
Is this Egyptian beer?

233
00:09:13,346 --> 00:09:15,511
[Found some Egyptian beer]
I think so. It has a pyramid on it.

234
00:09:15,511 --> 00:09:16,472
But…!

235
00:09:16,472 --> 00:09:17,872
[What if we sold beer to the princes...?]
Selling beer too…!

236
00:09:17,873 --> 00:09:19,911
Wait, it would be cool!

237
00:09:19,912 --> 00:09:21,256
[That’s a great idea]
Should we buy one and sell it?

238
00:09:21,257 --> 00:09:22,975
- Yeah, I think it's a good idea!
- Say that it's Egyptian beer.

239
00:09:22,976 --> 00:09:24,811
(For Sale)
Let's get one of these.

240
00:09:25,311 --> 00:09:26,078
[Big bro’s treat]
What do you want to drink?

241
00:09:26,079 --> 00:09:27,745
(For Home Use)
I'll pick one of these and one of those.

242
00:09:27,746 --> 00:09:29,287
[They each pick a drink they want]
Hey, is it possible to get that one?

243
00:09:29,288 --> 00:09:31,078
- Okay, okay.
- I'm just so curious.

244
00:09:31,182 --> 00:09:32,981
[Don't sell what I bought you tomorrow]
You can’t sell this tomorrow, okay? The one I bought you.

245
00:09:32,982 --> 00:09:36,045
Oh…I don't…Backstab.

246
00:09:36,046 --> 00:09:37,871
[Merchant YOHAN's main sales product]
You really can't!

247
00:09:37,872 --> 00:09:40,245
Promise me.

248
00:09:40,883 --> 00:09:43,411
[Lastly, let's buy magnets!]
Let's buy magnets. Magnets!

249
00:09:43,911 --> 00:09:46,678
[Wrapping up with
the travel shopping basics]

250
00:09:47,288 --> 00:09:48,678
Thank you.

251
00:09:48,978 --> 00:09:50,545
[Let's take a picture]
Thank you. Okay.

252
00:09:51,445 --> 00:09:53,874
[All purchases done!]
Thank you! Thank you!

253
00:09:53,875 --> 00:09:55,078
Thank you!

254
00:09:55,474 --> 00:09:56,378
That’s it, that’s it!

255
00:09:56,379 --> 00:09:59,545
[This was the paupers' tale from last night]
Thank you! Oh, thank you!

256
00:10:01,479 --> 00:10:04,678
Wow, but...it's so much prettier
seeing it during the daytime!

257
00:10:04,679 --> 00:10:07,478
I heard it sprinkled
a little last night.

258
00:10:07,479 --> 00:10:09,845
LEETEUK, didn't you say that before?

259
00:10:10,145 --> 00:10:11,782
It rains
when a precious guest arrives.

260
00:10:11,782 --> 00:10:12,878
Oh!

261
00:10:12,878 --> 00:10:14,694
[We are those precious guests…!]
Precious guests!

262
00:10:14,695 --> 00:10:15,911
So, we're the precious guests!

263
00:10:16,297 --> 00:10:17,711
Oh, but DAWN…

264
00:10:17,712 --> 00:10:21,278
[DAWN keeps on being a precious guest]
He’s never looked tired since he got here.

265
00:10:21,746 --> 00:10:23,911
Your Highnesses,
did you sleep well?

266
00:10:23,912 --> 00:10:25,265
[Energy fully recharged]
I slept like a baby.

267
00:10:25,266 --> 00:10:27,378
[The best part of traveling]
When you travel,

268
00:10:27,379 --> 00:10:28,978
[Shopping]
you can't leave out shopping!

269
00:10:28,978 --> 00:10:29,745
- Right.
- Right.

270
00:10:29,745 --> 00:10:32,978
[Staff] There's no other time to shop,
so we prepared this for you.

271
00:10:33,678 --> 00:10:38,111
[With the goods they hunted down themselves,]
The paupers have personally sought out goods

272
00:10:38,878 --> 00:10:41,211
[the real precious guests are coming]
and will be selling them to you today.

273
00:10:41,576 --> 00:10:44,090
If something catches your eye,
you can buy it

274
00:10:44,091 --> 00:10:46,578
- at a reasonable price out of your own pockets.
- Out of pocket!

275
00:10:47,978 --> 00:10:49,278
Assalamu alaikum!

276
00:10:49,279 --> 00:10:50,871
Korea!

277
00:10:50,872 --> 00:10:53,345
My friend!

278
00:10:56,098 --> 00:10:57,671
We're here to sell goods!

279
00:10:57,672 --> 00:10:58,978
Hello, hello!

280
00:10:59,978 --> 00:11:02,045
But this is great!

281
00:11:02,046 --> 00:11:03,478
We don't even have to go there!

282
00:11:03,479 --> 00:11:04,711
Assalamu alaikum!

283
00:11:04,878 --> 00:11:06,911
Assalamu alaikum!

284
00:11:06,912 --> 00:11:09,711
[The merchants are here]
Assalamu alaikum!

285
00:11:09,804 --> 00:11:12,671
- Assalamu alaikum!
- Oh, what?

286
00:11:12,679 --> 00:11:13,678
Assalamu alaikum!

287
00:11:13,679 --> 00:11:15,883
[Shocking visuals]
They're basically locals now.

288
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:17,079
Assalamu alaikum!

289
00:11:17,079 --> 00:11:18,692
[Led by the local resident, Mr. SHIN]
Assalamu alaikum!

290
00:11:18,692 --> 00:11:19,845
Hello, hello!

291
00:11:20,338 --> 00:11:22,038
[the paupers appear in perfect attire]
My friend!

292
00:11:22,039 --> 00:11:23,991
[the merchants appear in perfect attire]
Why do paupers look so good?

293
00:11:23,992 --> 00:11:25,504
- One dollar, one dollar!
- You look really good in those!

294
00:11:25,645 --> 00:11:27,545
[Satisfied princes]
My friend, my friend!

295
00:11:27,765 --> 00:11:28,811
Hold on, hold on.

296
00:11:28,812 --> 00:11:31,345
Your outfits are totally different!

297
00:11:31,346 --> 00:11:33,478
Aren't those stage costumes?!

298
00:11:33,479 --> 00:11:35,093
[More so today,]
Oh, what? He's Michael Jackson!

299
00:11:35,094 --> 00:11:36,575
[Michael JOHNNY is shining]
Since I don't know when I'd be a prince again.

300
00:11:36,576 --> 00:11:37,676
Oh, what? You look so cool!

301
00:11:37,677 --> 00:11:40,082
[Both fully dressed up, but totally different groups]
LEETEUK…What's with the shoes? Oof!

302
00:11:41,054 --> 00:11:42,845
How are the three of you
blending in here so perfectly already?

303
00:11:42,846 --> 00:11:43,937
[Feeling the class divide]
I slept so well.

304
00:11:43,946 --> 00:11:46,045
[So infuriating]

305
00:11:46,345 --> 00:11:47,645
[Staff] Princes...

306
00:11:47,646 --> 00:11:48,245
Yes?

307
00:11:48,246 --> 00:11:50,345
[Oh, right. I'm a pauper]
Yes? Oh, no.

308
00:11:50,346 --> 00:11:51,945
The people in front of you

309
00:11:51,946 --> 00:11:53,445
are merchants of the Nile River.

310
00:11:53,446 --> 00:11:56,045
[Merchants of the Nile]
Oh!

311
00:11:56,046 --> 00:12:00,178
They came to sell you
some fine goods,

312
00:12:00,179 --> 00:12:02,469
[Enjoy your shopping]
so carefully listen to their pitches,

313
00:12:02,470 --> 00:12:05,145
[with the merchants of the Nile]
and buy what you want.

314
00:12:06,588 --> 00:12:07,968
- Has the boat set off?
- Wow!

315
00:12:13,945 --> 00:12:19,211
[The Merchants of the Nile]

316
00:12:26,078 --> 00:12:29,311
[CHAPTER.4]
[The eyes cannot rise above the eyebrows]

317
00:12:32,045 --> 00:12:33,911
It's kind of like…
a department store…

318
00:12:33,912 --> 00:12:36,088
[Personal shoppers for the princes]
That's right, with the VIPs sitting around like this,

319
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:37,478
they explain each item, one by one.

320
00:12:37,878 --> 00:12:39,978
But you seem to be
quite successful merchants.

321
00:12:39,979 --> 00:12:41,073
Oh, really?

322
00:12:41,074 --> 00:12:42,778
Your outfits are really pretty.

323
00:12:42,779 --> 00:12:44,771
I'm even more excited
because they said the items are tailored for us.

324
00:12:44,772 --> 00:12:45,685
- Yeah, that's right.
- Yes.

325
00:12:46,171 --> 00:12:47,590
[So, who'll be the first merchant?]
Who’s going to sell first?

326
00:12:47,591 --> 00:12:49,283
Go ahead
and introduce your item first.

327
00:12:49,284 --> 00:12:50,390
[Merchant YOHAN takes the stage!]
I’ll go first then.

328
00:12:50,391 --> 00:12:51,978
- Wow, you have a lot!
- Yes, yes.

329
00:12:52,211 --> 00:12:53,174
Did you actually go
and buy these yourself?

330
00:12:53,175 --> 00:12:54,911
- We bought all of these ourselves.
- For real.

331
00:12:55,284 --> 00:12:58,911
[YOHAN] But for me…
You two might not know,

332
00:12:58,912 --> 00:13:01,411
but I really bought items
that are tailored just for each of you!

333
00:13:01,412 --> 00:13:02,973
- Is it a pigeon?
- Really?

334
00:13:02,974 --> 00:13:05,078
But we might not buy it.

335
00:13:05,086 --> 00:13:06,952
- Oh, but you'll have no choice but to buy it!
- Oh really?

336
00:13:07,045 --> 00:13:08,345
Oh, I'm excited now.

337
00:13:10,011 --> 00:13:11,011
[Customer]
DAWN.

338
00:13:11,378 --> 00:13:12,610
[Diving right into his strategy]
Oh, it's me?

339
00:13:12,611 --> 00:13:13,870
You said this outfit was pretty.

340
00:13:13,871 --> 00:13:14,678
Yeah, it’s really gorgeous.

341
00:13:14,679 --> 00:13:16,790
[So, I prepared it for you]
So, I…!

342
00:13:16,791 --> 00:13:18,078
Oh!

343
00:13:19,278 --> 00:13:21,645
[Dramatically unveiled a gold & black cloth]
Wow, it looks like a designer item!

344
00:13:22,011 --> 00:13:23,911
(Swoosh)
So I prepared this for you.

345
00:13:23,912 --> 00:13:25,478
[DAWN]
Wow!

346
00:13:25,479 --> 00:13:27,478
[What do you think?]
Wow!

347
00:13:27,675 --> 00:13:29,479
I said it was really pretty!

348
00:13:29,512 --> 00:13:31,711
[Galabeya]
(Egyptian traditional outfit)

349
00:13:32,245 --> 00:13:34,611
[Just Egypt itself,
with golden patterns shining bright]

350
00:13:34,612 --> 00:13:36,944
[and even a simple neckline]

351
00:13:38,078 --> 00:13:41,345
[These two princes
don't seem that interested]

352
00:13:41,977 --> 00:13:44,070
- But the color is so…!
- In gold! Gold!

353
00:13:44,071 --> 00:13:45,979
[Meanwhile, Prince DAWN seems interested]
It's so fancy.

354
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:47,385
But why does it
have short sleeves?

355
00:13:47,385 --> 00:13:49,478
- It's hot in Egypt, you know?
- Oh, because it's hot!

356
00:13:49,479 --> 00:13:52,057
[With Merchant YOHAN's full-on sales pitch,]
You gotta wear this at least once when you’re in Egypt.

357
00:13:52,058 --> 00:13:53,172
So, yes.

358
00:13:53,173 --> 00:13:55,145
[will his wallet open for the very first item…?]
I prepared this one.

359
00:13:55,146 --> 00:13:56,611
Ohhh...

360
00:13:56,612 --> 00:13:59,445
[YOHAN’s outfit]
The absolute worst of the worst!

361
00:13:59,745 --> 00:14:03,845
This... YOHAN definitely
shouldn’t go into business.

362
00:14:03,846 --> 00:14:05,999
[One-line review]
That outfit is probably

363
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:10,911
[A time-capsule outfit buried in a closet]
something I'd find when I'm moving.

364
00:14:11,946 --> 00:14:14,845
[YOHAN, you’re doomed]
The absolute worst of the worst!

365
00:14:14,846 --> 00:14:15,878
And I…

366
00:14:15,879 --> 00:14:17,572
While buying this yesterday,
I came across a heartbreaking story.

367
00:14:17,572 --> 00:14:18,686
[With a heartbreaking story included]
Yes, yes.

368
00:14:18,686 --> 00:14:20,071
[The second item]
Actually…

369
00:14:20,072 --> 00:14:23,345
Actually...
I wanted to give this to LEETEUK…

370
00:14:24,245 --> 00:14:26,285
[Ladybugs in Egypt mean]
Ladybugs in Egypt mean…

371
00:14:26,286 --> 00:14:28,089
[Good Luck]
Ladybugs represent luck.

372
00:14:28,090 --> 00:14:29,078
- Oh, really?
- Yes.

373
00:14:29,079 --> 00:14:30,369
[Actually, dung beetles (scarabs) mean luck]
Since they represent luck,

374
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:31,511
I…

375
00:14:31,512 --> 00:14:33,811
At one of the local shops,
with their own hands,

376
00:14:33,812 --> 00:14:35,578
they crafted this for 3 days!

377
00:14:35,579 --> 00:14:36,878
- Handmade?
- Handmade!

378
00:14:36,879 --> 00:14:37,711
Handmade is great.

379
00:14:37,871 --> 00:14:39,772
And I bought it
at a really high price.

380
00:14:39,773 --> 00:14:41,078
I really bought it
at a high price.

381
00:14:41,079 --> 00:14:43,345
- It's a handmade ladybug?
- A handmade ladybug…

382
00:14:43,346 --> 00:14:45,845
- with your initials engraved too!
- Oh, for real?

383
00:14:46,078 --> 00:14:48,711
[Merchant YOHAN's secret weapon]

384
00:14:49,311 --> 00:14:50,878
[The only one in this world]

385
00:14:50,879 --> 00:14:53,678
[A special LEETEUK edition]
Oh, for real?

386
00:14:53,679 --> 00:14:55,445
- So I got it done…
- Oh, for real?

387
00:14:55,446 --> 00:14:57,277
But then SHINDONG broke it!

388
00:14:57,278 --> 00:14:58,778
Oh, what? What? What?

389
00:14:59,284 --> 00:15:00,678
Oh, what? What? What?

390
00:15:01,577 --> 00:15:02,645
- Oh, what?
- How did that happen?

391
00:15:02,679 --> 00:15:05,478
[No, like, how…??]
If you look closely…

392
00:15:06,212 --> 00:15:09,411
[After ambitiously buying the stone slab]
Thank you! Bye-bye!

393
00:15:11,045 --> 00:15:13,678
(Ran into SHINDONG)
But this is seriously amazing.

394
00:15:13,679 --> 00:15:14,478
What is it?

395
00:15:14,479 --> 00:15:15,883
This is just…

396
00:15:17,711 --> 00:15:19,877
I hope LEETEUK will buy it.

397
00:15:19,879 --> 00:15:21,184
- Is it clothes?
- No.

398
00:15:21,185 --> 00:15:22,945
- Oh, an engraved tablet?
- Yeah, an engraved tablet.

399
00:15:22,945 --> 00:15:24,178
[Happily opened up his shopping bag!]

400
00:15:26,880 --> 00:15:27,778
- Oh! Oh! Oh!
- Oh!

401
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:28,978
[Crack!]
Oh! Oh! Oh!

402
00:15:32,645 --> 00:15:33,278
SHINDONG!!!!!

403
00:15:34,678 --> 00:15:35,678
SHINDONG…!

404
00:15:37,571 --> 00:15:40,304
[Stone slab completely shattered]

405
00:15:40,711 --> 00:15:41,778
[along with YOHAN's mental state]

406
00:15:41,779 --> 00:15:44,378
Ugh, SHINDONG, seriously…!

407
00:15:47,145 --> 00:15:50,178
No, I…
I didn't try to grab it!

408
00:15:50,978 --> 00:15:52,978
Sigh…I was so sad…

409
00:15:53,645 --> 00:15:54,778
[Summary]
Thud! And then…

410
00:15:54,779 --> 00:15:56,778
Crack!

411
00:15:56,779 --> 00:15:58,374
"AGH!!!!"

412
00:15:58,375 --> 00:15:59,945
I was like, "SHINDONG!!!!"

413
00:15:59,946 --> 00:16:01,078
I just screamed.

414
00:16:01,511 --> 00:16:03,845
YOHAN,
you need to be on variety shows.

415
00:16:03,846 --> 00:16:06,578
[According to SHINDONG]
But, everything YOHAN does is so funny.

416
00:16:06,579 --> 00:16:09,845
[For that, too, is a blessing from the variety gods…]
I'm so jealous! I'm so jealous of that talent!

417
00:16:10,266 --> 00:16:11,661
- Oh my god!
- Hey, what do we do about this?

418
00:16:11,662 --> 00:16:14,383
- What do I do?
- What do we do about this?

419
00:16:14,384 --> 00:16:15,945
[A stone slab, once broken,
can never be undone…]

420
00:16:20,004 --> 00:16:22,178
(Full of resentment)

421
00:16:22,179 --> 00:16:23,345
Oh, but, this…

422
00:16:23,346 --> 00:16:24,778
If it didn't crack,
I think I would've bought it.

423
00:16:24,779 --> 00:16:26,478
(Agrees)
It'd be so nice to display in your house.

424
00:16:26,479 --> 00:16:27,863
I think it'd be so pretty.

425
00:16:27,863 --> 00:16:29,378
- So…!
- So…?

426
00:16:29,379 --> 00:16:31,245
- So…!
- So…?

427
00:16:32,011 --> 00:16:33,662
[It's not a lucky dung beetle]
It's not a ladybug,

428
00:16:33,663 --> 00:16:35,711
but a symbol of Egypt…!

429
00:16:35,978 --> 00:16:37,245
- What is it?
- Cleopatra…!

430
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:39,578
[A substitute product]
Oh!!

431
00:16:40,145 --> 00:16:42,745
[Hand-carved with care]

432
00:16:43,245 --> 00:16:45,345
[Capturing the craftsman’s spirit]

433
00:16:45,578 --> 00:16:48,611
[A stone slab of Cleopatra]

434
00:16:48,899 --> 00:16:50,956
- This is nice!
- It's pretty!

435
00:16:50,964 --> 00:16:51,878
- This is nice!
- Yes.

436
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:53,445
Does it have my initials?

437
00:16:53,446 --> 00:16:54,678
The initials…

438
00:16:54,679 --> 00:16:56,878
[It's a long story…]
After seeing me break it,

439
00:16:56,879 --> 00:17:00,581
the vendor got so mad!

440
00:17:00,582 --> 00:17:02,411
["You...! My masterpiece...!"]
He was like that,

441
00:17:02,645 --> 00:17:04,678
[You, follow me]
and then he told me to come.

442
00:17:04,679 --> 00:17:05,777
And I got dragged off like this.

443
00:17:06,117 --> 00:17:07,686
He's really mad right now…

444
00:17:07,687 --> 00:17:08,418
I got dragged off.

445
00:17:08,945 --> 00:17:10,878
- But he was very generous…
- Yeah.

446
00:17:11,545 --> 00:17:13,175
[I’ll give you a new one!]
and he'll give me a replacement!

447
00:17:13,176 --> 00:17:13,978
Oh!

448
00:17:15,578 --> 00:17:16,775
- Like this!
- Okay, okay!

449
00:17:16,776 --> 00:17:17,962
- Like this, okay?
- Okay!

450
00:17:17,963 --> 00:17:18,745
Sorry, sorry.

451
00:17:18,745 --> 00:17:19,478
(Grin)
[Hold it tightly]

452
00:17:19,478 --> 00:17:21,811
Thank you!
Sorry!

453
00:17:23,067 --> 00:17:25,078
But asking for initials too
would be a bit shameless.

454
00:17:25,079 --> 00:17:26,978
(Well done, YOHAN)
That’s right, exactly.

455
00:17:26,979 --> 00:17:29,563
[The second item has no initials, but a story]
So, it's symbolic! It's Cleopatra!

456
00:17:29,564 --> 00:17:31,877
- Oh, this is really nice.
- So I brought this. So that's that!

457
00:17:31,878 --> 00:17:33,978
[Even the princes are happy with it]
You bought everything really well.

458
00:17:34,269 --> 00:17:35,578
- And this too…!
- JOHNNY style.

459
00:17:35,579 --> 00:17:38,478
This one's for JOHNNY and DAWN.

460
00:17:38,479 --> 00:17:40,445
[Another secret weapon
for DAWN and JOHNNY]

461
00:17:40,446 --> 00:17:42,739
[Egyptian beer]
Shouldn't we try Egyptian beer at least once?

462
00:17:42,746 --> 00:17:44,711
- We drank it yesterday, though?
- We drank it yesterday.

463
00:17:44,712 --> 00:17:47,078
- We drank it yesterday.
- So you did.

464
00:17:47,079 --> 00:17:49,645
Then I'll drink it instead!

465
00:17:49,646 --> 00:17:50,945
But was it good?

466
00:17:50,946 --> 00:17:52,245
Yeah, it was good!
It was really good!

467
00:17:52,246 --> 00:17:54,211
Then, you could drink it again…!

468
00:17:54,212 --> 00:17:55,252
We have cold ones.

469
00:17:55,253 --> 00:17:56,376
Oh, cold ones…

470
00:17:56,377 --> 00:17:57,345
There’s a ton of them over there

471
00:17:57,346 --> 00:17:59,675
[The freezer...? May I...?]
I’ll just pop it in the freezer for a bit.

472
00:17:59,676 --> 00:18:00,795
- We've got so much in stock.
- YOHAN.

473
00:18:00,796 --> 00:18:02,645
Have you ever seen ice
since coming here?

474
00:18:02,646 --> 00:18:03,545
Ice...?

475
00:18:03,546 --> 00:18:04,584
- Where's the ice…?
- Ice!

476
00:18:04,585 --> 00:18:05,478
Where's the ice?

477
00:18:05,479 --> 00:18:06,792
There's so much ice here.

478
00:18:06,793 --> 00:18:09,078
- I'll stick this in ice for a little bit!
- Oh, yeah, yeah.

479
00:18:09,079 --> 00:18:10,145
(Chilling)

480
00:18:10,146 --> 00:18:12,683
- That's that, and…
- Actually, this was his kicker.

481
00:18:12,684 --> 00:18:13,973
[His failed secret weapons]

482
00:18:13,974 --> 00:18:14,878
So, you…you already drank it…

483
00:18:14,879 --> 00:18:16,088
He's totally off guard right now.

484
00:18:16,588 --> 00:18:18,769
I guess I have nothing
to buy from Merchant YOHAN.

485
00:18:18,770 --> 00:18:20,278
- Oh, right.
- I have nothing to buy.

486
00:18:20,279 --> 00:18:21,874
[There was a necklace too]
It was seriously pretty.

487
00:18:21,875 --> 00:18:23,786
- A necklace?
- Yes, it was a necklace.

488
00:18:23,787 --> 00:18:24,911
Oh, man.

489
00:18:25,265 --> 00:18:27,080
- Where'd it go?
- My neck does feel a bit empty right now.

490
00:18:27,081 --> 00:18:27,976
It disappeared…

491
00:18:27,977 --> 00:18:28,745
Yeah.

492
00:18:28,746 --> 00:18:30,759
[Unfortunately, that's it for Merchant YOHAN's items]
Alright then, we got it.

493
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:33,211
- You were witty about it.
- We'll come back after looking at other stuff.

494
00:18:34,169 --> 00:18:35,468
[Merchant YOHAN’s Sales List]
[Galabeya (traditional Egyptian outfit): 1]

495
00:18:35,469 --> 00:18:37,697
[Scarab Stone Slab: Damaged]
[Cleopatra Stone Slab: 1]

496
00:18:37,698 --> 00:18:39,445
[Egyptian Beer: 1]
[Ankh Necklace: Missing]

497
00:18:39,446 --> 00:18:41,681
[And…]
Just as you said, the beer was the kicker.

498
00:18:41,682 --> 00:18:44,145
[Very busy behind the scenes...]
Yeah, the beer was the game changer.

499
00:18:44,871 --> 00:18:47,104
[The Merchant in Blue]

500
00:18:47,274 --> 00:18:48,270
It reminded me of that.

501
00:18:48,271 --> 00:18:50,410
[When it comes to this man…]
In the past, SHINDONG was on a home shopping show,

502
00:18:50,411 --> 00:18:51,686
[SUPER JUNIOR's SHINDONG, a home shopping superstar]
and he sold everything.

503
00:18:51,687 --> 00:18:53,745
[with 2.1 billion won in sales in just 50 minutes]
It didn't sell out for no reason.

504
00:18:53,746 --> 00:18:55,878
[With just one move,]
When SHINDONG wore it and posed,

505
00:18:55,879 --> 00:18:59,078
[everything instantly sells out]
that size was the first to be sold out.

506
00:18:59,365 --> 00:19:02,278
After seeing that, I thought,

507
00:19:02,285 --> 00:19:04,884
[The epitome of "sold out"]
He's just the Sold-Out King, no matter what he does.

508
00:19:05,778 --> 00:19:09,578
[And now,
the "Sold Out" legend makes his move]

509
00:19:09,579 --> 00:19:11,388
Alright, my friend.

510
00:19:11,389 --> 00:19:13,911
- Assalamu alaikum!
- Very nice! Assalamu alaikum!

511
00:19:13,912 --> 00:19:16,278
- You really seem like the ultimate merchant.
- He seems like a local.

512
00:19:16,279 --> 00:19:18,878
[The aura of a master merchant]
I've prepared items tailored for you.

513
00:19:18,879 --> 00:19:21,993
[The "Sold Out" merchant in blue's first item is?]
I'll first start with something very simple.

514
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:22,978
SHINDONG looks so good
in outfits like that.

515
00:19:22,979 --> 00:19:25,894
This might seem small, but this…!

516
00:19:25,895 --> 00:19:27,645
It's something you can have

517
00:19:27,646 --> 00:19:29,378
- Wow, this guy…!
- for an affordable price.

518
00:19:29,379 --> 00:19:30,693
(Shyly clasping his two hands)
Oh, it's small, it's small.

519
00:19:30,694 --> 00:19:32,845
But it looks better when it's small.

520
00:19:32,846 --> 00:19:33,878
Alright, everyone.

521
00:19:33,879 --> 00:19:38,278
There are many legends
about animals in Egypt.

522
00:19:38,279 --> 00:19:39,211
But like YOHAN said,

523
00:19:39,212 --> 00:19:42,045
the scarab has the meaning
of "guiding your path forward"...

524
00:19:42,046 --> 00:19:43,378
[Ladybug]
Wasn’t it a ladybug?

525
00:19:43,379 --> 00:19:44,178
It's a scarab.

526
00:19:44,179 --> 00:19:46,182
- Didn't he say it was a ladybug earlier?
- I think it was a scarab.

527
00:19:46,403 --> 00:19:47,778
[Scarab]
Oh, it's a dung beetle! A dung beetle!

528
00:19:47,779 --> 00:19:49,083
[Dung beetle]
So, it was a dung beetle!

529
00:19:49,084 --> 00:19:50,278
It’s a dung beetle, a dung beetle

530
00:19:50,279 --> 00:19:51,673
[Scarab]
This little dung beetle

531
00:19:51,674 --> 00:19:53,975
[Symbolizes rebirth, vitality, and fresh starts]
lights the path ahead of me!

532
00:19:53,976 --> 00:19:56,361
[Known to bring luck and success]
So, this is the first gift I prepared for you all.

533
00:19:56,362 --> 00:19:58,781
The incredible gift is this!

534
00:19:58,782 --> 00:19:59,978
…is this!

535
00:20:01,178 --> 00:20:03,211
[What’s that?]

536
00:20:03,212 --> 00:20:05,211
[What is it?]

537
00:20:07,297 --> 00:20:09,897
Hand-carved from wood…!

538
00:20:09,898 --> 00:20:10,692
What is it?

539
00:20:10,692 --> 00:20:13,530
[A scarab miniature]
The cutest little dung beetle!

540
00:20:13,546 --> 00:20:15,863
Keep this at home,
and it'll guide the way to your future!

541
00:20:15,864 --> 00:20:17,378
[It looks like puffed corn...?]
It looks like that, puffed corn.

542
00:20:17,379 --> 00:20:18,378
- Oh!
- Yeah!

543
00:20:18,379 --> 00:20:20,778
You may think that way, but…

544
00:20:21,245 --> 00:20:21,811
It's a very tiny…

545
00:20:21,812 --> 00:20:23,011
[Puffed rice?]
Isn’t it puffed rice?

546
00:20:23,084 --> 00:20:25,088
(Ignoring)
Made with a one-to-one ratio…

547
00:20:25,089 --> 00:20:27,005
- Oh, one-to-one!
- Yes, made to actual size…!

548
00:20:27,006 --> 00:20:28,280
- Hand-carved from wood…
- But this is just

549
00:20:28,286 --> 00:20:29,679
[Purchase Inquiry #01]
too small.

550
00:20:29,679 --> 00:20:31,487
[Because it's so tiny,]
Even if I put this in my home,

551
00:20:31,488 --> 00:20:34,111
[my guests won't know what it is]
I would have to explain why it's there.

552
00:20:34,112 --> 00:20:35,083
[Response Submitted #01]
There's fun in looking for it!

553
00:20:35,084 --> 00:20:36,344
[A product that’s fun to find]
Yeah, yes.

554
00:20:36,346 --> 00:20:38,172
"Hey, there's something
in this house that I bought from Egypt!"

555
00:20:38,173 --> 00:20:38,863
"Try to find it!"

556
00:20:38,864 --> 00:20:40,183
- Then, they'll start searching, right?
- Yeah, yeah.

557
00:20:40,184 --> 00:20:41,778
[Found it!!!]
And then… "I found it!!"

558
00:20:41,779 --> 00:20:43,478
[Your Future]
"I’ll light up the path ahead of you."

559
00:20:43,479 --> 00:20:45,544
[Purchase Inquiry #02]
But the thing is, if I leave this at home,

560
00:20:45,545 --> 00:20:47,093
[It's so small]
my dog will think it's a puffed corn snack

561
00:20:47,093 --> 00:20:48,512
[that my dog might swallow it]
and just eat it.

562
00:20:48,512 --> 00:20:50,175
[Response Submitted #02]
Then, for our non-dog owner,

563
00:20:50,175 --> 00:20:51,812
[Not recommended for dog owners]
JOHNNY…!

564
00:20:51,812 --> 00:20:53,490
[JOHNNY, this is yours!]
Let me show it to you!

565
00:20:53,491 --> 00:20:54,411
Wow, he really just
wiggled his way out of that one!

566
00:20:54,412 --> 00:20:55,845
- This is the first…
- I've seen plenty.

567
00:20:55,846 --> 00:20:57,910
[Quick and smooth]
We'll move to the second item! The second item is…

568
00:20:57,911 --> 00:20:59,173
(Shocked by the size of the first item)
It's really so tiny.

569
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:01,178
This is just…So…

570
00:21:01,179 --> 00:21:03,578
You did pay money for this, right?

571
00:21:03,845 --> 00:21:06,545
[Come on, now…]

572
00:21:07,178 --> 00:21:07,878
Gift?

573
00:21:07,879 --> 00:21:08,378
[Yeah.]

574
00:21:08,379 --> 00:21:09,378
Thank you!

575
00:21:09,379 --> 00:21:10,811
[Paid money for it…]
Oh!

576
00:21:10,812 --> 00:21:12,311
[Nope]
Thank you.

577
00:21:12,312 --> 00:21:13,995
[A true master merchant, who paid nothing for it]
It feels like he just picked it off the street.

578
00:21:13,995 --> 00:21:15,811
- No.
- No? It's handmade?

579
00:21:16,379 --> 00:21:18,778
Oh, this…
It's expensive…

580
00:21:18,779 --> 00:21:19,745
It looks factory-made, though?

581
00:21:19,746 --> 00:21:22,090
[Lying like it’s his second nature]
I actually sat there and bargained for it.

582
00:21:22,091 --> 00:21:23,782
[As the controversy rages on…]
Sorry, but I think you bought beer,

583
00:21:23,783 --> 00:21:26,212
- and they gave you this as a freebie.
- No, no!

584
00:21:26,212 --> 00:21:27,278
Okay, the second item!

585
00:21:27,279 --> 00:21:29,389
So when you guys travel,

586
00:21:29,789 --> 00:21:30,878
do you ever like…

587
00:21:30,879 --> 00:21:32,578
[Q. A must-buy travel souvenir?]
"Oh, I definitely need to get this when I visit this country!"

588
00:21:32,579 --> 00:21:34,378
There's that thing you have to buy
when you visit a certain country!

589
00:21:34,379 --> 00:21:34,978
A keyring.

590
00:21:34,979 --> 00:21:37,378
No way it's a fridge…magnet…

591
00:21:37,379 --> 00:21:39,500
[Magnet]
I prepared magnets! You need this!

592
00:21:39,501 --> 00:21:41,178
- You have to have this!
- Oh, you have to have it!

593
00:21:41,179 --> 00:21:43,080
Whenever you travel,

594
00:21:43,081 --> 00:21:44,973
you always buy a magnet.

595
00:21:44,974 --> 00:21:46,064
I prepared three kinds for you!

596
00:21:46,065 --> 00:21:47,678
But don't magnets usually
not stick to modern refrigerators?

597
00:21:47,679 --> 00:21:50,278
- The material these days is a bit…
- The fridge is…

598
00:21:50,279 --> 00:21:52,578
…The magnets stick to the sides.

599
00:21:52,579 --> 00:21:53,778
You’re supposed to
stick them on the side panel...

600
00:21:53,779 --> 00:21:54,778
[The sides don't show for built-in fridges]
But mine's a built-in fridge.

601
00:21:54,779 --> 00:21:57,111
Oh, really?
If it's a built-in fridge, it'll stick fine on the front.

602
00:21:57,112 --> 00:21:57,845
It won't stick, it won't.

603
00:21:57,846 --> 00:21:58,578
Really?

604
00:21:58,579 --> 00:22:00,611
And I also hate having
stuff all over.

605
00:22:00,612 --> 00:22:01,963
[Well…! That’s a bummer...]
I like things neat and tidy.

606
00:22:01,964 --> 00:22:03,378
- Oh, really?
- But seriously…

607
00:22:04,078 --> 00:22:05,911
They're so funny.

608
00:22:05,912 --> 00:22:06,579
Anyway, three kinds...

609
00:22:06,580 --> 00:22:08,678
So, I brought three kinds
thinking about you three!

610
00:22:08,679 --> 00:22:10,811
[A set of 3 magnets]

611
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:12,344
Oh!

612
00:22:12,345 --> 00:22:13,287
This one's pretty.

613
00:22:13,288 --> 00:22:16,287
[All eyes on the first magnet]
First, you all know this, right?

614
00:22:16,288 --> 00:22:17,711
- Pretty!
- What is it?

615
00:22:17,712 --> 00:22:18,678
Who is this guy…?

616
00:22:18,679 --> 00:22:19,945
- Pharaoh...
- It's Pharaoh.

617
00:22:20,211 --> 00:22:21,578
[What do you mean by "this guy"?]
It's the Pharaoh!

618
00:22:21,579 --> 00:22:23,511
- You bought it without knowing!
- No!

619
00:22:23,681 --> 00:22:25,894
I brought the Pharaoh
to sell to you!

620
00:22:25,895 --> 00:22:28,378
[1. The Pharaoh, brought for sale]
First, number 1!

621
00:22:28,379 --> 00:22:29,387
Now, number 2

622
00:22:29,388 --> 00:22:30,184
[2. Manus]
Manus!

623
00:22:30,185 --> 00:22:31,681
Oh, this is a must-have.

624
00:22:31,681 --> 00:22:32,587
You’ve seen this a lot, right?

625
00:22:32,588 --> 00:22:34,578
[This is Bastet, the guardian god]

626
00:22:34,745 --> 00:22:36,378
- This is a must-have.
- This is a must-have!

627
00:22:36,379 --> 00:22:38,480
You all have dogs at home, right?

628
00:22:38,481 --> 00:22:39,678
[It is a cat goddess]
We do, we do!

629
00:22:39,679 --> 00:22:41,573
(He's right about nothing)
Just think of it as your pet dog

630
00:22:41,574 --> 00:22:42,711
and take a look at it.

631
00:22:42,712 --> 00:22:44,578
[And the last one]
And the third one is this!

632
00:22:44,579 --> 00:22:45,768
I'm sure
you've seen this symbol a lot.

633
00:22:45,769 --> 00:22:46,678
This is pretty!

634
00:22:46,678 --> 00:22:50,178
- It's kind of like Chrome Hearts.
- This one's nice, right?

635
00:22:50,179 --> 00:22:50,876
It looks like a designer brand.

636
00:22:50,877 --> 00:22:53,273
[3. Ankh, the Key of Life]
It could easily pass as a designer brand.

637
00:22:53,274 --> 00:22:55,082
Yes, so I brought
three different types of magnets.

638
00:22:55,083 --> 00:22:56,183
Three different types of magnets.

639
00:22:56,184 --> 00:22:57,476
[The more they hear, the more they want the magnets]
But the third one's really pretty.

640
00:22:57,478 --> 00:22:59,497
I prepared these three types.
And next!

641
00:22:59,498 --> 00:23:01,478
[The second item:
Three types of magnets with a botched intro]

642
00:23:01,479 --> 00:23:03,411
- But SHINDONG…
- Yes?

643
00:23:03,412 --> 00:23:05,456
These items are a lot
smaller compared to your size.

644
00:23:05,457 --> 00:23:06,474
There are more coming.

645
00:23:06,475 --> 00:23:07,469
- Oh, really?
- Alright, everyone!

646
00:23:07,470 --> 00:23:09,878
[Now]
Alright, everyone!

647
00:23:09,879 --> 00:23:13,078
[Something big is coming]

648
00:23:13,079 --> 00:23:14,578
Oh!

649
00:23:15,772 --> 00:23:17,078
Oh!

650
00:23:19,045 --> 00:23:20,345
It's what we saw on the bus!

651
00:23:20,346 --> 00:23:21,378
When you’re on a trip,

652
00:23:21,379 --> 00:23:23,045
you’ve gotta grab
at least one of these.

653
00:23:23,046 --> 00:23:25,078
I prepared three of them,
thinking of you three.

654
00:23:25,945 --> 00:23:29,378
[A set of three pyramids]

655
00:23:29,379 --> 00:23:31,081
[And not just any pyramids]
These aren’t your average pyramids.

656
00:23:31,082 --> 00:23:32,982
There was a merchant sitting there.

657
00:23:32,983 --> 00:23:33,978
He was squatting

658
00:23:33,979 --> 00:23:35,399
[Carved all day long by the merchant]
and carving it all day long.

659
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,478
Oh, is this handmade too?

660
00:23:36,479 --> 00:23:37,883
[It’s handmade, folks]
It’s handmade! Handmade!

661
00:23:37,884 --> 00:23:39,245
Originally, it's silky smooth.

662
00:23:39,246 --> 00:23:41,178
Silky smooth, silky smooth.

663
00:23:41,179 --> 00:23:43,245
Flat, flat!
Flat, flat!

664
00:23:43,246 --> 00:23:44,811
(Flat)
Laid out nice and flat…!

665
00:23:45,189 --> 00:23:46,645
Laid out nice and flat…!

666
00:23:46,646 --> 00:23:48,582
[This shop knows how to sell!]
Wow, this merchant's really good.

667
00:23:48,583 --> 00:23:50,345
- This is fun.
- Yes, yes.

668
00:23:50,346 --> 00:23:51,556
- Now, everyone…
- Is it made of wood?

669
00:23:51,557 --> 00:23:52,811
No, this is

670
00:23:52,812 --> 00:23:53,678
stone! Stone!

671
00:23:53,679 --> 00:23:54,711
- Can I touch it?
- Stone, stone.

672
00:23:54,712 --> 00:23:55,978
- Wait! Before you touch it!
- Oh, yes?

673
00:23:55,979 --> 00:23:57,474
Everyone, here…

674
00:23:57,475 --> 00:23:58,978
He's keeping me
on the edge of my seat!

675
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,211
Everyone,

676
00:24:00,212 --> 00:24:01,078
there's a secret here.

677
00:24:01,079 --> 00:24:01,645
[Eager]
What kind of secret?

678
00:24:01,646 --> 00:24:02,511
[So eager]
He's good at this, he's good!

679
00:24:02,512 --> 00:24:03,978
[Also eager]
You just can't say no to this!

680
00:24:03,979 --> 00:24:06,078
I knew you'd want it, so I had

681
00:24:06,079 --> 00:24:07,478
[Custom initial engraving for each person]
your initials engraved!

682
00:24:07,479 --> 00:24:09,045
- Wow!
- Now!

683
00:24:09,046 --> 00:24:10,489
- Here we go!
- Wow!

684
00:24:10,490 --> 00:24:14,078
- I had your names engraved!
- Wow! Wow!

685
00:24:14,079 --> 00:24:16,187
- This is insane! Totally insane!
- Wow!

686
00:24:16,188 --> 00:24:17,183
[I love it]
Your names are engraved here!

687
00:24:17,184 --> 00:24:17,970
JOHNNY!

688
00:24:17,971 --> 00:24:18,870
- LEETEUK!
- LEETEUK!

689
00:24:18,871 --> 00:24:19,711
- And DAWN.
- DAWN.

690
00:24:20,111 --> 00:24:21,278
And on the second line,

691
00:24:21,279 --> 00:24:23,078
- in this country's language…
- No way!

692
00:24:23,079 --> 00:24:25,174
[Even engraved the hieroglyphs]
It says J-O-H-N.

693
00:24:25,175 --> 00:24:26,210
- Oh, it's Arabic?
- Seriously, wow!

694
00:24:26,211 --> 00:24:27,766
[On the last line…]
And!

695
00:24:27,767 --> 00:24:30,545
[Remembering Luxor...]
Bought in "Luxor 2026"!

696
00:24:30,546 --> 00:24:32,185
- This is meaningful!
- This is a good one!

697
00:24:32,186 --> 00:24:33,445
You’ve gotta take this with you.

698
00:24:33,446 --> 00:24:35,711
[Too good for just the princes to keep]
It feels wrong that it’s only for the three of us.

699
00:24:36,073 --> 00:24:38,278
[Nervous]
You've got to take this.

700
00:24:38,279 --> 00:24:39,388
[It’s not over yet]
But this isn't everything!

701
00:24:39,389 --> 00:24:40,982
- There's more…!
- Yes, yes.

702
00:24:40,983 --> 00:24:42,796
- He sells really well.
- He's really good at this.

703
00:24:42,797 --> 00:24:43,978
There's only one of these!

704
00:24:43,979 --> 00:24:45,079
[This item is a one of a kind]
I’m tempted.

705
00:24:45,080 --> 00:24:46,508
There's only one of these.

706
00:24:46,509 --> 00:24:47,561
[A statue of Anubis]
This was a bit pricey,

707
00:24:47,561 --> 00:24:48,773
so I couldn't buy many of them.

708
00:24:48,774 --> 00:24:50,776
- Sorry, I’m short on cash.
- But yeah, it does look expensive.

709
00:24:50,777 --> 00:24:51,781
- Is it made of stone?
- It's stone.

710
00:24:51,782 --> 00:24:53,175
Feel free to touch the stone.

711
00:24:53,611 --> 00:24:54,275
(Go ahead and touch as much as you want)
It's stone.

712
00:24:54,276 --> 00:24:55,887
- Handmade, handmade?
- It's handmade.

713
00:24:55,888 --> 00:24:57,196
- Everything here is handmade.
- Wow, so pretty!

714
00:24:57,197 --> 00:24:58,190
But this is really pretty.

715
00:24:58,191 --> 00:24:59,282
- So pretty.
- I picked the white one on purpose.

716
00:24:59,283 --> 00:25:02,145
[Rare item: A white Anubis]
Black is usually the symbolic color of Anubis.

717
00:25:02,146 --> 00:25:04,483
[The master merchant's items are soaring in popularity]
I feel like he might actually start an auction.

718
00:25:04,484 --> 00:25:05,485
Yeah, this is so nice.

719
00:25:05,485 --> 00:25:06,657
This one’s a bit pricey.

720
00:25:06,658 --> 00:25:07,984
Sorry,
this one's kind of expensive.

721
00:25:07,985 --> 00:25:09,545
Oh, but now…

722
00:25:09,546 --> 00:25:10,078
There’s more...?

723
00:25:10,079 --> 00:25:12,045
Everyone, just placing
things around isn't enough.

724
00:25:12,046 --> 00:25:14,178
- You need something to hang on the wall!
- Oh!

725
00:25:14,462 --> 00:25:15,978
So, I prepared this.

726
00:25:16,170 --> 00:25:17,578
[Not a fan of this kind of thing...]
I’m not really into this kind of thing.

727
00:25:18,465 --> 00:25:20,385
- LEETEUK, you don't like things hanging or sticking…
- I hate sticking things up.

728
00:25:20,386 --> 00:25:21,778
(No clutter, please)
and hammering nails on the walls.

729
00:25:21,779 --> 00:25:23,078
- You don't have to hammer nails in.
- I don't need to hammer anything?

730
00:25:23,079 --> 00:25:24,445
[Don’t worry]
It’s lightweight, so just stick it up.

731
00:25:24,446 --> 00:25:25,487
I prepared three sheets!

732
00:25:25,488 --> 00:25:26,978
[3 types of papyrus artwork]
Here's the first one!

733
00:25:26,979 --> 00:25:28,578
The second one!

734
00:25:29,072 --> 00:25:31,372
And the third one!
But everyone,

735
00:25:31,855 --> 00:25:33,275
[There are two effects here...?]
there are actually two effects.

736
00:25:33,276 --> 00:25:34,445
What kind of effects?

737
00:25:34,446 --> 00:25:35,878
[One item]
One piece

738
00:25:35,879 --> 00:25:37,190
[Two images]
can turn into two pieces!

739
00:25:37,191 --> 00:25:38,178
- Everyone…
- How? How?

740
00:25:38,179 --> 00:25:39,945
It's too bright right now,

741
00:25:39,946 --> 00:25:41,778
but this…glows in the dark!

742
00:25:41,779 --> 00:25:42,978
This glows in the dark.

743
00:25:43,111 --> 00:25:43,778
Huh??

744
00:25:43,779 --> 00:25:44,876
- It glows in the dark.
- It glows in the dark?

745
00:25:44,877 --> 00:25:45,678
Everyone, it glows in the dark.

746
00:25:45,679 --> 00:25:46,789
- Really?
- Really!

747
00:25:46,790 --> 00:25:47,551
Can I see it like this?

748
00:25:47,552 --> 00:25:48,578
[One minute! One minute!]
Wait a moment, wait a moment!

749
00:25:48,579 --> 00:25:49,745
[Eager]
Hold your horses!

750
00:25:50,177 --> 00:25:51,107
[Super intriguing feature:]
Everyone, it glows in the dark.

751
00:25:51,108 --> 00:25:52,474
[Glows in the dark]
He could sell insurance for a living.

752
00:25:52,475 --> 00:25:54,378
- This is really amazing.
- Wow.

753
00:25:54,692 --> 00:25:56,377
- Oh, are you seeing it for the first time too?
- Yes.

754
00:25:56,678 --> 00:25:57,963
[Seems quite suspicious]
[Shining a light onto the image]

755
00:25:57,964 --> 00:25:58,769
Whoa!

756
00:25:58,770 --> 00:26:00,778
It seems like
he's decoding something.

757
00:26:00,779 --> 00:26:03,445
[Staring hard]

758
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:04,711
Wow...

759
00:26:04,712 --> 00:26:05,711
He's seriously…

760
00:26:05,712 --> 00:26:06,794
sparking my curiosity…

761
00:26:06,795 --> 00:26:07,878
He's like a magician!

762
00:26:07,879 --> 00:26:10,745
[Oh, you merchant, you…!]
Oh! Magic! Oh, magician!

763
00:26:10,746 --> 00:26:11,978
Now, look at it in the dark.
Look at it.

764
00:26:11,979 --> 00:26:13,263
(Ready for the demo)
Now, look at it in the dark.

765
00:26:13,264 --> 00:26:14,278
Look at it in the dark.

766
00:26:15,078 --> 00:26:16,045
Can you see the glow?

767
00:26:16,046 --> 00:26:17,311
I think I can see it…

768
00:26:17,312 --> 00:26:18,445
Everyone, you can see it!

769
00:26:18,452 --> 00:26:20,544
(Is it not…? Am I hallucinating…?)
I don't think it is glowing, but it also is…?

770
00:26:20,545 --> 00:26:22,382
[Lemme borrow this outfit]
Excuse me, can I borrow this outfit for a moment?

771
00:26:22,383 --> 00:26:23,689
[What are you doing]
Oh, sorry, but I can't let you do that!

772
00:26:23,690 --> 00:26:25,545
[using someone else's stuff?]
This is…! Come on! This is…

773
00:26:25,546 --> 00:26:27,280
[A dark curtain setup]
Now, put this over your head.

774
00:26:27,281 --> 00:26:28,112
Take a look!

775
00:26:28,278 --> 00:26:29,878
Go inside! Go inside!

776
00:26:29,978 --> 00:26:31,678
(This is gonna be fun)

777
00:26:32,545 --> 00:26:35,511
[When you block the light with darkness,]

778
00:26:35,811 --> 00:26:39,045
[a whole new image is seen]

779
00:26:39,145 --> 00:26:41,211
[It's glowing! Wow!]
Oh, it's there! It's there!

780
00:26:41,778 --> 00:26:44,688
[You can see it!! It shows!!!!]
It’s here, it’s here!

781
00:26:44,689 --> 00:26:45,578
So, two types of images!

782
00:26:45,579 --> 00:26:47,679
[A set of three papyrus images]
One piece

783
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:50,310
[Glow-in-the-dark (proven)]
shows two different images! Two images!

784
00:26:50,312 --> 00:26:51,081
We're selling this as a set!

785
00:26:51,082 --> 00:26:53,378
[Matching item (Blackout curtain for the demo)]
You need to cover your head, so this will be a set.

786
00:26:53,379 --> 00:26:55,678
[Desperate]
Two images in one! There are two images!

787
00:26:55,911 --> 00:26:58,378
If you put this in your room

788
00:26:58,379 --> 00:26:59,289
and turn off the lights!

789
00:26:59,290 --> 00:27:00,978
When you turn off the lights,
the whole new image will glow!

790
00:27:00,979 --> 00:27:04,710
[A glowing mural world will unfold before your eyes]
And that image will be of the Egyptian mural!

791
00:27:04,711 --> 00:27:06,678
As if my room
just transformed into Egypt!

792
00:27:06,679 --> 00:27:07,378
Exactly.

793
00:27:07,379 --> 00:27:10,181
[One image that'll take you on a trip to Egypt]
The only thing that'll transform your home into Egypt!

794
00:27:10,182 --> 00:27:11,764
My room’s gonna
get so mysterious!

795
00:27:11,765 --> 00:27:13,595
Right?
Visible even in the dark.

796
00:27:13,596 --> 00:27:14,545
[Lastly!!!!!!]
And last, but not least!

797
00:27:14,546 --> 00:27:15,511
And last, but not least!

798
00:27:15,512 --> 00:27:16,400
- There's more?
- It just keeps coming!

799
00:27:16,401 --> 00:27:17,711
- There's more?
- Lastly, everyone…

800
00:27:17,712 --> 00:27:20,181
[A large supply of items fit for a large company-level master merchant]
Did you have the most money to start with?

801
00:27:20,183 --> 00:27:20,745
No.

802
00:27:20,746 --> 00:27:23,377
- So how will you carry this when you buy it?
- What?

803
00:27:23,378 --> 00:27:24,961
- You're gonna need a bag to carry it.
- Oh, a bag!

804
00:27:24,962 --> 00:27:28,078
[A savvy merchant’s final move]
I've prepared three different kinds of bags.

805
00:27:28,079 --> 00:27:29,545
- Oh, pretty! The bags are pretty!
- Egypt bags!

806
00:27:29,546 --> 00:27:30,872
[Three types of Egypt eco bags]
They're pretty, right?

807
00:27:30,873 --> 00:27:31,772
I totally need something like this.

808
00:27:31,773 --> 00:27:33,671
Okay, number 1, number 2, number 3.

809
00:27:33,672 --> 00:27:34,745
Everyone, you love bags.

810
00:27:34,746 --> 00:27:37,075
[Perfect to take on walks with my dog, Simkoong]
I carry something like that when I go to doggy daycare!

811
00:27:37,076 --> 00:27:39,587
Eco bags!
Eco bags are all the rage these days!

812
00:27:39,588 --> 00:27:40,764
[Oozing with Egyptian vibes]
But since you visited Egypt,

813
00:27:40,765 --> 00:27:41,771
you need to bring out
that Egyptian vibe!

814
00:27:41,772 --> 00:27:43,776
- Are these eco-friendly? Eco bags?
- Yes, they're eco bags.

815
00:27:43,777 --> 00:27:45,178
But with designer bag vibes!

816
00:27:45,179 --> 00:27:46,545
[Dior…?]
It looks kind of like Dior, right?

817
00:27:46,546 --> 00:27:48,090
[Convincing]
It's pretty, it's pretty!

818
00:27:48,090 --> 00:27:48,897
It has Dior vibes.

819
00:27:48,898 --> 00:27:51,170
- It's pretty.
- When you go to the grocery store, just put it on!

820
00:27:51,171 --> 00:27:52,485
- Wow!
- It does have that vibe!

821
00:27:52,486 --> 00:27:54,684
[The luxurious master merchant]
But this one’s not bad either.

822
00:27:54,684 --> 00:27:56,745
It has that vibe, right?

823
00:27:56,746 --> 00:28:00,181
JISUNG said on the side,
"Oh, that's pretty nice."

824
00:28:00,182 --> 00:28:01,311
"Oh, that's pretty nice."

825
00:28:01,562 --> 00:28:03,869
(A fan of large companies)
Wow, he's really good.

826
00:28:03,877 --> 00:28:05,710
But, this is pretty nice.

827
00:28:05,711 --> 00:28:08,511
I... hit a wall there.

828
00:28:08,512 --> 00:28:10,072
I wanted to buy it too.

829
00:28:10,073 --> 00:28:12,073
There was actually
something I wanted to buy.

830
00:28:12,979 --> 00:28:14,578
[But JISUNG...]
The pyramid one!

831
00:28:14,579 --> 00:28:16,778
[You’re a merchant here...]
If my name were engraved on it, I'd definitely buy it.

832
00:28:16,779 --> 00:28:18,711
I would've bought it
at double the price.

833
00:28:19,178 --> 00:28:19,986
(Dibs)
Oh, that's pretty nice.

834
00:28:19,987 --> 00:28:21,411
I've prepared
all of these items for you.

835
00:28:21,412 --> 00:28:22,675
(Eyeing the prize)

836
00:28:22,676 --> 00:28:24,069
You can check them out later.

837
00:28:24,070 --> 00:28:25,769
[I'll see you later when you make your purchase]
This is really nice. He did really well.

838
00:28:25,777 --> 00:28:28,078
- Pretty good, right?
- I really gotta give this to him.

839
00:28:28,079 --> 00:28:30,287
[With great applause, Merchant SHINDONG finishes his pitch]
There were a few things I liked.

840
00:28:30,288 --> 00:28:31,778
That's right, that's right.
Everyone, you want it, right?

841
00:28:31,779 --> 00:28:33,459
[Merchant SHINDONG Sales List:]
This is why he told me to go first.

842
00:28:33,460 --> 00:28:34,567
[Scarab Miniature: 1]
[Magnets: 3]

843
00:28:34,568 --> 00:28:35,694
[Pyramid Statues: 3]
[Anubis Statue: 1]

844
00:28:35,695 --> 00:28:36,878
[Glow-in-the-Dark Papyrus Artworks: 3]
[Eco Bags: 3]

845
00:28:36,879 --> 00:28:38,685
[After the master merchant swept through like a storm...]
Hey, let’s pile these here together.

846
00:28:38,686 --> 00:28:40,745
- You want them, don't you?
- Let's clear this all out.

847
00:28:41,377 --> 00:28:42,045
Oh, this…

848
00:28:42,046 --> 00:28:45,711
[Fidgeting nervously]
I almost cleared away the beer.

849
00:28:45,711 --> 00:28:47,978
[This merchant looks particularly sad]
I almost cleared away the beer.

850
00:28:47,979 --> 00:28:50,745
I thought it was the one
we drank yesterday.

851
00:28:51,111 --> 00:28:52,100
But SHINDONG,
you really bought good items.

852
00:28:52,101 --> 00:28:53,578
You bought them well.

853
00:28:53,945 --> 00:28:56,511
[Deep breaths]

854
00:28:57,711 --> 00:28:58,288
Alright!

855
00:28:58,992 --> 00:29:00,499
Alright!

856
00:29:01,112 --> 00:29:02,145
[With this order]
He must feel so much pressure.

857
00:29:02,146 --> 00:29:04,845
Imagine how much
pressure he's feeling.

858
00:29:04,846 --> 00:29:07,311
[I must overcome…
the hurdle of the master merchant]

859
00:29:07,312 --> 00:29:08,078
Alright!

860
00:29:08,278 --> 00:29:09,278
Hey, this is actually fun!

861
00:29:09,279 --> 00:29:11,378
It's great being a prince!

862
00:29:11,963 --> 00:29:13,744
[You gotta make it big in life]
Hey, Egypt is great!

863
00:29:13,903 --> 00:29:16,671
My time as a prince yesterday
was too short!

864
00:29:16,679 --> 00:29:17,893
[Former princes put on a whole show]
I don’t even remember being a prince.

865
00:29:17,894 --> 00:29:19,545
I seriously don't remember at all.

866
00:29:19,778 --> 00:29:22,778
[Meanwhile, prince satisfaction is at 10,000%]
I feel great because the setting is great!

867
00:29:22,779 --> 00:29:23,478
Alright!

868
00:29:24,511 --> 00:29:26,778
You just said "Alright" for the 6th time!

869
00:29:26,779 --> 00:29:27,378
Alright!

870
00:29:27,778 --> 00:29:30,245
[Finally revealing Merchant JISUNG's goods]
Ladies and gentlemen… Oh, okay.

871
00:29:30,246 --> 00:29:31,908
I take pride in this.

872
00:29:32,878 --> 00:29:34,311
Among all these items here,

873
00:29:34,312 --> 00:29:36,772
[The priciest one]
I brought the most expensive thing.

874
00:29:36,772 --> 00:29:37,377
It's the most expensive?

875
00:29:37,378 --> 00:29:39,978
[Coincidentally]
I looked at the princes' necks,

876
00:29:39,979 --> 00:29:42,011
and for people who have the means,
your necks are bare.

877
00:29:42,012 --> 00:29:44,378
Your necks seem
kind of bare today, so…

878
00:29:44,379 --> 00:29:45,878
- But I'm wearing two necklaces.
- I'm wearing a ton of stuff.

879
00:29:46,578 --> 00:29:48,045
[Dangling]
But, but…!

880
00:29:48,046 --> 00:29:49,911
But! But…!

881
00:29:49,912 --> 00:29:51,178
Those are all in neutral tones.

882
00:29:51,179 --> 00:29:53,980
[The secret weapon that'll make the princes glow]
Today, I’ve got something that’ll make you all shine bright.

883
00:29:53,981 --> 00:29:55,378
Colorful…

884
00:29:55,845 --> 00:29:56,767
And sparkly?

885
00:29:56,768 --> 00:29:58,645
- And sparkly!
- Oh!

886
00:29:58,646 --> 00:30:01,511
[So excited]
Wow, but the color is beautiful.

887
00:30:01,869 --> 00:30:03,310
I'll do it for you.
Your hands are shaking too much.

888
00:30:03,311 --> 00:30:05,289
I'm very…nervous…

889
00:30:05,290 --> 00:30:06,677
Oh, it must be that!

890
00:30:08,146 --> 00:30:12,378
[Opal glowing with a mysterious blue light]

891
00:30:13,245 --> 00:30:16,145
[combined with the pure simplicity of silver]

892
00:30:16,845 --> 00:30:20,045
[A pyramid opal necklace]

893
00:30:20,678 --> 00:30:22,578
It'd look so good
during the summer.

894
00:30:22,579 --> 00:30:24,478
(Likes it already)
The color is very refreshing.

895
00:30:24,479 --> 00:30:25,778
Honestly, for me,

896
00:30:25,779 --> 00:30:27,545
I don't want to sell this.

897
00:30:27,546 --> 00:30:28,711
Got it.

898
00:30:28,712 --> 00:30:30,811
- But! But! But!
- Got it, got it. Yes, but?

899
00:30:30,812 --> 00:30:32,378
- But!
- But?

900
00:30:32,379 --> 00:30:34,478
[Something he'd also like to keep]
But it's because I want to take this home.

901
00:30:34,479 --> 00:30:36,245
This is actually…

902
00:30:36,471 --> 00:30:37,953
There are usually
multiple pendants, right?

903
00:30:37,954 --> 00:30:39,787
[The one and only pyramid pendant]
But there was only one of these.

904
00:30:39,788 --> 00:30:41,789
- But it does look like a designer brand.
- Yes.

905
00:30:41,790 --> 00:30:43,967
[With opal]
And the stone inside is opal.

906
00:30:43,968 --> 00:30:45,444
- Oh!
- Opal!

907
00:30:45,445 --> 00:30:46,678
- Everything's handmade, right?
- Yes.

908
00:30:46,679 --> 00:30:47,778
This one isn’t handmade.

909
00:30:47,779 --> 00:30:48,683
Because this is just

910
00:30:48,684 --> 00:30:50,564
[A thing from nature…???]
a thing from nature itself.

911
00:30:50,565 --> 00:30:51,569
What is "a thing from nature"?

912
00:30:51,570 --> 00:30:52,963
- I brought nature itself to you!
- Nature-made.

913
00:30:52,964 --> 00:30:54,511
- Nature-made.
- Yes, nature made this.

914
00:30:54,512 --> 00:30:56,395
Is the chain silver?

915
00:30:56,396 --> 00:30:57,078
The chain’s silver too.

916
00:30:57,079 --> 00:30:58,178
Just in case,

917
00:30:58,179 --> 00:31:00,178
I slept wearing it to see
if I'd get a metal allergy.

918
00:31:00,179 --> 00:31:01,478
(Metal allergy test complete)
But I had no reaction at all.

919
00:31:01,479 --> 00:31:02,378
Oh, wait.

920
00:31:02,379 --> 00:31:04,710
Then it's "used"!

921
00:31:04,711 --> 00:31:06,194
[A "Marketplace" vendor sneaks into the Nile?]
Why are you selling used stuff?

922
00:31:06,195 --> 00:31:08,177
- No, wait…!
- Why did you come wearing that?

923
00:31:08,178 --> 00:31:09,778
It lost value! It lost value!

924
00:31:09,779 --> 00:31:11,888
LEETEUK hates used stuff!

925
00:31:11,889 --> 00:31:13,178
I like brand new things!

926
00:31:13,179 --> 00:31:14,411
It's secondhand! Secondhand!

927
00:31:14,911 --> 00:31:17,311
But!
That means it’s proven its quality!

928
00:31:17,883 --> 00:31:19,478
I still don't like used stuff!

929
00:31:19,678 --> 00:31:20,878
Why do you think
royal food testers existed?

930
00:31:20,879 --> 00:31:22,878
They existed to check
if the food was poisoned or not!

931
00:31:22,879 --> 00:31:24,686
- Then if you were selling underwear…
- So for this…!

932
00:31:24,687 --> 00:31:26,375
- To check if it causes an allergic reaction or not…
- You don't know if it causes an allergic reaction!

933
00:31:26,389 --> 00:31:28,104
[Is this a rap battle or what?]
I wore this underwear yesterday!

934
00:31:28,105 --> 00:31:29,745
[Taster JISUNG VS Brand New LEETEUK]
It’s exactly the same as this!

935
00:31:29,978 --> 00:31:31,078
[That has poison]
Maybe that's poisoned!

936
00:31:31,079 --> 00:31:32,745
[This one does not]
But this has no poison, seriously.

937
00:31:33,045 --> 00:31:33,844
[Raises eyebrow]
This is poisoned?

938
00:31:33,845 --> 00:31:35,411
That beer might be poisoned…!

939
00:31:35,412 --> 00:31:37,378
[Come on, now!]
It's not even open! What are you talking about?

940
00:31:37,379 --> 00:31:39,011
[JISUNG the unstoppable seller]
This has no poison.

941
00:31:39,511 --> 00:31:41,245
- He's roasting someone else's item…!
- This has no poison.

942
00:31:41,246 --> 00:31:43,578
- Wow, he's really overreaching.
- I know, right?

943
00:31:43,845 --> 00:31:44,687
(Stay calm, stay calm)

944
00:31:44,688 --> 00:31:46,095
Please continue!

945
00:31:46,096 --> 00:31:47,178
We'll give you
more time to explain.

946
00:31:47,878 --> 00:31:48,664
P-please... b-buy it...

947
00:31:48,665 --> 00:31:50,278
What?
Oh, you want us to buy it?

948
00:31:50,279 --> 00:31:51,678
I…I'm a pauper-pauper.

949
00:31:51,679 --> 00:31:53,685
[A sudden strategy shift]
A pauper-pauper. A two-times pauper.

950
00:31:53,686 --> 00:31:55,544
- Oh, a pauper-pauper.
- Today, you're a bit…

951
00:31:55,546 --> 00:31:57,378
Prince-prince.
Pauper-pauper.

952
00:31:57,379 --> 00:32:00,278
- Oh, my maternal instincts!
- He's triggering our maternal instincts!

953
00:32:00,478 --> 00:32:02,078
- For the pauper-pauper's items, from what I can tell…
- I'm torn.

954
00:32:02,079 --> 00:32:03,378
I think the prince-prince needs to buy it.

955
00:32:03,778 --> 00:32:04,378
And…

956
00:32:04,379 --> 00:32:05,378
There's more! There's more!

957
00:32:05,379 --> 00:32:06,278
- And…
- Huh? What is it?

958
00:32:06,765 --> 00:32:07,610
Huh, huh?

959
00:32:07,611 --> 00:32:09,272
[The item that disappeared!]
Hey, this is mine, huh?!

960
00:32:09,273 --> 00:32:10,945
Hey, this is mine!

961
00:32:11,865 --> 00:32:13,552
(Let me check)
This is really…

962
00:32:13,560 --> 00:32:14,408
Wow…

963
00:32:14,409 --> 00:32:15,781
[Embarrassed]
Oh, it's not.

964
00:32:15,782 --> 00:32:17,089
What’s up with YOHAN?

965
00:32:17,090 --> 00:32:18,594
- There was another one?
- There's another one.

966
00:32:18,595 --> 00:32:19,483
Yeah, there was another one.

967
00:32:19,484 --> 00:32:21,183
[The second necklace he bought in secret?]
He didn't even tell us about it!

968
00:32:21,184 --> 00:32:22,276
Actually, this too is...

969
00:32:22,277 --> 00:32:23,990
[Nature-made again]
all from nature

970
00:32:23,991 --> 00:32:24,970
- Huh?
- It's natural.

971
00:32:24,971 --> 00:32:26,670
[Raw stone necklace]
You can tell it's natural from the color.

972
00:32:26,671 --> 00:32:28,611
- There's no pattern, and it's a bit irregular.
- Hey, this…

973
00:32:28,791 --> 00:32:31,778
[That... looks familiar?]
Hey, this…Isn't it that?

974
00:32:31,779 --> 00:32:32,545
It's that!

975
00:32:32,779 --> 00:32:34,579
[Dung beetle, is that you…?]
Oh, yeah, it's the same thing!

976
00:32:34,580 --> 00:32:35,672
Oh, uh, hmm?

977
00:32:35,673 --> 00:32:37,245
- Oh... seriously...
- But what’s this, and what’s that then?

978
00:32:37,762 --> 00:32:39,587
- This is…
- Is it a stone?

979
00:32:39,588 --> 00:32:41,578
The origin is unknown.

980
00:32:41,579 --> 00:32:43,476
[Gone]
Then I can't buy it!

981
00:32:43,477 --> 00:32:46,045
- That’s how rare it is!
- I need to know to buy it.

982
00:32:46,411 --> 00:32:48,411
But honestly,
JISUNG’s turban is pretty.

983
00:32:48,412 --> 00:32:49,745
[Surprised]
The hat?

984
00:32:49,746 --> 00:32:51,545
- Oh…This…This, you can't…
- His outfits are so pretty.

985
00:32:51,546 --> 00:32:53,694
- Are you gonna buy this?
- "This, you can't…"

986
00:32:53,695 --> 00:32:54,581
[Rather rigid]
Not this one.

987
00:32:54,582 --> 00:32:55,788
This is sponsored,
so he can't sell it.

988
00:32:55,789 --> 00:32:57,287
[The hat is not for resale]
Oh, it's sponsored.

989
00:32:57,288 --> 00:32:58,144
Got it.

990
00:32:58,145 --> 00:33:00,088
[That’s it for Merchant JISUNG's items!]
We checked everything. Please hand that here.

991
00:33:00,088 --> 00:33:01,479
Oh, thank you.

992
00:33:01,479 --> 00:33:02,978
Oh, but you did a good job.

993
00:33:02,979 --> 00:33:04,167
[Merchant JISUNG's Sales List]
I know, right?

994
00:33:04,168 --> 00:33:05,173
[Pyramid Opal Necklace: 1]
I worked really hard to buy everything.

995
00:33:05,174 --> 00:33:07,778
[Raw Stone Necklace: 1]
Thinking of gifting them to all of you.

996
00:33:08,345 --> 00:33:11,411
[The merchants of the Nile
begin selling their goods]

997
00:33:11,511 --> 00:33:12,878
[Staff] Yesterday, the merchants

998
00:33:12,879 --> 00:33:14,775
[The merchants bought items on the same budget]
all used the same amount

999
00:33:14,776 --> 00:33:16,878
to buy all the items here.

1000
00:33:16,879 --> 00:33:20,778
[The merchants will make the first offers]
The merchants will name the price first.

1001
00:33:20,973 --> 00:33:22,878
[Likes collecting cute travel souvenirs]
For me, when I travel,

1002
00:33:22,886 --> 00:33:26,285
I still tend to pick up
those charming little things.

1003
00:33:26,404 --> 00:33:29,604
I have this rule, like,
“If it’s worth this price, I’ll buy it.”

1004
00:33:29,612 --> 00:33:31,711
[Not the type to haggle aggressively]
No matter where I go, it'll be around this price.

1005
00:33:31,845 --> 00:33:32,911
When I saw
what they bought from the market,

1006
00:33:32,912 --> 00:33:34,378
"Wow, it must have been
so much fun…"

1007
00:33:34,578 --> 00:33:35,961
I love going to markets!

1008
00:33:35,962 --> 00:33:37,245
Just wandering around
and exploring the market.

1009
00:33:37,378 --> 00:33:40,011
[Satisfied by the merchants’ taste]
But honestly, everyone did a great job finding stuff.

1010
00:33:40,012 --> 00:33:42,145
Except YOHAN...

1011
00:33:42,278 --> 00:33:43,878
The rich are more tight-fisted!

1012
00:33:43,879 --> 00:33:45,478
A penny saved is a penny earned!

1013
00:33:45,479 --> 00:33:46,981
Every penny counts!!!

1014
00:33:46,982 --> 00:33:47,911
Just like that,

1015
00:33:47,912 --> 00:33:50,111
[A wallet that's hard to even pry open]
I want to save.

1016
00:33:50,478 --> 00:33:53,145
[Mission: Break even!]
My goal is to at least get my money back!

1017
00:33:53,411 --> 00:33:54,678
Maybe bump it up to 100,000 won?

1018
00:33:54,679 --> 00:33:55,778
If I can up it that much.

1019
00:33:56,011 --> 00:33:57,878
[Reality check: At least break even]
Let’s just hit that 90,000 won mark.

1020
00:33:58,145 --> 00:33:59,378
[It’s all about the energy]
This is pure momentum!

1021
00:33:59,379 --> 00:34:00,978
This is all about the energy!

1022
00:34:01,178 --> 00:34:02,945
You can't give them
a chance to talk!

1023
00:34:02,946 --> 00:34:03,978
I’m just gonna keep

1024
00:34:03,979 --> 00:34:05,778
[Aiming to sell everything with sheer momentum]
saying the good things about it!

1025
00:34:05,945 --> 00:34:07,678
[Staff] If I can tell you
about the Egyptian pound exchange rate…

1026
00:34:07,679 --> 00:34:08,878
To convert to Korean won,

1027
00:34:08,879 --> 00:34:10,078
[Easy calculation: 1 pound = around 30 won]
you just multiply by 30

1028
00:34:10,079 --> 00:34:10,910
30?

1029
00:34:10,911 --> 00:34:12,878
[1 pound = around 30 won]
So 1,000 Egyptian pounds is about 30,000 won.

1030
00:34:12,879 --> 00:34:14,778
[1,000 pounds = around 30,000 won]
Oh, so 1,000 is 30,000 won.

1031
00:34:14,978 --> 00:34:16,145
Just how much did you get?

1032
00:34:16,146 --> 00:34:18,045
I think JISUNG
kind of got ripped off.

1033
00:34:18,211 --> 00:34:19,483
[A modest list compared to the other vendors]
I know, right?

1034
00:34:19,484 --> 00:34:21,345
From what I can tell,

1035
00:34:21,346 --> 00:34:24,201
I bet he got played by the vendors
because he seems too innocent.

1036
00:34:24,202 --> 00:34:25,245
Seriously, how much
did you spend to buy it…

1037
00:34:25,246 --> 00:34:27,011
Let's hear the prices!

1038
00:34:27,012 --> 00:34:28,411
[The first sale]
It was the very first item.

1039
00:34:28,412 --> 00:34:29,978
Merchant YOHAN.

1040
00:34:29,979 --> 00:34:31,378
That outfit!

1041
00:34:31,611 --> 00:34:32,745
[Egyptian traditional outfit]
How much is this?

1042
00:34:32,746 --> 00:34:34,311
It's so cool.

1043
00:34:34,845 --> 00:34:36,078
Oh, nice!

1044
00:34:36,079 --> 00:34:37,278
Oh, oh!

1045
00:34:37,279 --> 00:34:38,578
(Love it)
But I do kinda wanna buy it.

1046
00:34:38,579 --> 00:34:39,811
Oh, but I'm not shopping for me.

1047
00:34:40,978 --> 00:34:42,511
(You gonna buy it?)

1048
00:34:42,604 --> 00:34:44,471
[First, checking the price]

1049
00:34:44,478 --> 00:34:45,889
[0]
[650]

1050
00:34:45,889 --> 00:34:48,478
[650 pounds (about 19,500 won)]
He told the staff 650 pounds.

1051
00:34:48,949 --> 00:34:50,245
(Happiness Evangelist)
You happy, I’m happy.

1052
00:34:50,246 --> 00:34:51,095
[650]
[300]

1053
00:34:51,096 --> 00:34:52,778
[Let’s try cutting it in half first]

1054
00:34:52,779 --> 00:34:54,278
[Nope]
How about…

1055
00:34:54,279 --> 00:34:55,778
[550]
100 discount?

1056
00:34:55,779 --> 00:34:57,111
100 discount!

1057
00:34:57,345 --> 00:34:59,178
[Still too soon to compromise]
Oh, no, no! Okay.

1058
00:34:59,179 --> 00:35:00,211
[550]
[400]

1059
00:35:00,218 --> 00:35:01,817
(Reading the room)
Okay.

1060
00:35:01,978 --> 00:35:02,582
Happy, happy!

1061
00:35:02,583 --> 00:35:03,762
[400]
[500]

1062
00:35:03,763 --> 00:35:04,562
Wow!

1063
00:35:04,563 --> 00:35:06,078
[One tough Happiness Evangelist]
Between, between.

1064
00:35:06,079 --> 00:35:06,782
[500]
[450]

1065
00:35:06,783 --> 00:35:08,812
Let’s go with this, seriously!

1066
00:35:08,813 --> 00:35:09,612
[Deal!]

1067
00:35:09,618 --> 00:35:11,950
[Successfully haggled: 650 pounds / 450 pounds]
Okay, okay, okay, okay!

1068
00:35:12,111 --> 00:35:14,945
He really made it fun!

1069
00:35:15,878 --> 00:35:16,976
[Properly looking at it in detail]
Large size.

1070
00:35:16,977 --> 00:35:18,245
Yes, yes, yes.
Extra large.

1071
00:35:18,378 --> 00:35:19,978
I don't think
it's your personal color.

1072
00:35:19,979 --> 00:35:21,078
It's a large, though?

1073
00:35:21,079 --> 00:35:22,611
- A large size.
- Yeah.

1074
00:35:22,711 --> 00:35:24,478
I'll offer 1,200 pounds!

1075
00:35:24,479 --> 00:35:25,478
If it's 1,200 pounds…

1076
00:35:25,479 --> 00:35:26,988
[Buying price: 450 pounds]
Yes, 1,200 pounds.

1077
00:35:26,989 --> 00:35:28,878
[Selling price: 1,200 pounds]
36,000 won?

1078
00:35:28,879 --> 00:35:30,311
[Price increased to 2.7 times the original]
But 36,000 won is kinda pricey.

1079
00:35:30,312 --> 00:35:31,645
What?

1080
00:35:31,778 --> 00:35:32,978
When we go to Thailand,
we always buy stuff like this.

1081
00:35:32,979 --> 00:35:33,845
Oh, right!

1082
00:35:33,978 --> 00:35:36,275
If this were 3,000 or 5,000 won,

1083
00:35:36,276 --> 00:35:37,878
you'd have money left over.

1084
00:35:38,086 --> 00:35:40,111
[Like the Happiness Evangelist, he asks for a counteroffer]
Then please make an offer first for me.

1085
00:35:40,578 --> 00:35:41,378
I’m not making an offer.

1086
00:35:41,379 --> 00:35:42,311
No, no!

1087
00:35:43,978 --> 00:35:45,484
[DAWN is a smart shopper]
Good job, DAWN. You're good at this.

1088
00:35:45,485 --> 00:35:46,511
It's so my vibe.

1089
00:35:46,512 --> 00:35:47,411
[Hmm...]
I won't make any offer on this.

1090
00:35:47,412 --> 00:35:48,378
But, uh…

1091
00:35:48,445 --> 00:35:49,711
You really don't want it?

1092
00:35:49,712 --> 00:35:51,011
Let's hear him out for everything.
How much is this?

1093
00:35:51,012 --> 00:35:52,211
That’s a bit pricey.

1094
00:35:52,311 --> 00:35:53,281
[Cleopatra Stone Slab]
Oh yeah? How much exactly?

1095
00:35:53,282 --> 00:35:54,911
- I kind of want this one.
- At the market,

1096
00:35:54,912 --> 00:35:58,311
there were only a handful of people
who were working on this by hand.

1097
00:35:58,312 --> 00:35:59,811
(Handcrafted premium)
So I paid quite a bit more for this.

1098
00:35:59,812 --> 00:36:01,111
[Intrigued]
There’s definitely some value here.

1099
00:36:01,178 --> 00:36:02,278
So, how much?

1100
00:36:02,445 --> 00:36:03,678
Then, if I give you
a bit of a discount,

1101
00:36:03,838 --> 00:36:05,171
1,800 pounds.

1102
00:36:05,172 --> 00:36:06,481
[Selling price: 1,800 pounds]
That's around 50 to 60,000 won.

1103
00:36:06,495 --> 00:36:08,517
- Around 50,000 won.
- 50,000 won. Around there.

1104
00:36:09,111 --> 00:36:10,678
I bought it for 2,000 pounds.

1105
00:36:11,645 --> 00:36:12,845
[1,500]

1106
00:36:12,846 --> 00:36:14,865
[Around 45,000 won]
[Offered 1,500 pounds]

1107
00:36:14,865 --> 00:36:16,411
1,500 pounds, okay, okay.

1108
00:36:16,478 --> 00:36:17,878
[Emphasized 3 days of handcrafting]
Three days’ work!

1109
00:36:17,879 --> 00:36:19,145
Oh, you worked on it for three days.

1110
00:36:19,345 --> 00:36:21,378
[Handcrafted confirmed]
[Bought for 1,500 pounds]

1111
00:36:21,645 --> 00:36:23,178
(Really paid a lot for it)
This one was actually really expensive.

1112
00:36:23,179 --> 00:36:23,985
It's all good, but…

1113
00:36:23,986 --> 00:36:25,245
[A weight issue]
It’s way too heavy.

1114
00:36:25,246 --> 00:36:26,845
When you take it to Korea,

1115
00:36:26,846 --> 00:36:28,278
it'll make your suitcase heavier.

1116
00:36:28,279 --> 00:36:30,178
[A fragility issue]
And I'm afraid it'll break.

1117
00:36:30,179 --> 00:36:32,045
- It can break like this…
- Exactly.

1118
00:36:32,245 --> 00:36:33,178
I'll carry it!

1119
00:36:33,976 --> 00:36:35,878
- Oh, delivery service?
- A delivery service.

1120
00:36:35,879 --> 00:36:37,278
[Free shipping]
Delivery?

1121
00:36:37,279 --> 00:36:38,178
I'll carry it with me.

1122
00:36:38,179 --> 00:36:38,878
How much is the shipping?

1123
00:36:38,879 --> 00:36:40,778
[International shipping, but it’s free]
The shipping’s free.

1124
00:36:41,245 --> 00:36:43,545
- Oh, it can even be delivered!
- I'll carry it.

1125
00:36:43,546 --> 00:36:44,645
Not bad!

1126
00:36:44,646 --> 00:36:46,178
Wait, for just
these two items alone,

1127
00:36:46,179 --> 00:36:47,578
[Egyptian Traditional Outfit: 1,200 pounds]
the price is

1128
00:36:47,579 --> 00:36:49,089
[Cleopatra Stone Slab: 1,800 pounds]
way higher than I anticipated.

1129
00:36:49,090 --> 00:36:50,478
Then, from what I can tell,

1130
00:36:50,479 --> 00:36:52,511
- they must've gotten around 100,000 won.
- Yeah.

1131
00:36:52,678 --> 00:36:53,945
Then for the outfit…!

1132
00:36:53,946 --> 00:36:54,778
A mega sale!

1133
00:36:54,779 --> 00:36:56,178
- A mega sale!
- With the mega sale…

1134
00:36:56,311 --> 00:36:57,478
How much did I quote
earlier again?

1135
00:36:57,778 --> 00:36:58,578
(He's the seller)

1136
00:36:58,579 --> 00:36:59,763
(He's the customer)
1,200 pounds.

1137
00:36:59,764 --> 00:37:00,896
[Egyptian Traditional Outfit: 1,200 pounds]
I said it was 1,200 pounds, right?

1138
00:37:00,897 --> 00:37:02,145
Mega sale!

1139
00:37:02,146 --> 00:37:03,178
[Discounted price: 700 pounds]

1140
00:37:03,179 --> 00:37:04,378
[A flash sale]
I seriously can't go any lower.

1141
00:37:04,379 --> 00:37:05,611
- Seriously, 700 pounds!
- 21,000 won.

1142
00:37:05,711 --> 00:37:06,778
Even that’s pricey.

1143
00:37:06,779 --> 00:37:07,811
- Really?
- Yeah.

1144
00:37:07,812 --> 00:37:09,092
[Discounted price: 650 pounds]

1145
00:37:09,093 --> 00:37:10,986
[Expected fair price: 3,000 won - 5,000 won]
This should honestly be around 3,000 to 5,000 won.

1146
00:37:10,987 --> 00:37:12,711
- Isn't it a matter of whether it'll sell or not?
- 3…000 won?

1147
00:37:12,712 --> 00:37:14,578
I actually thought 10,000 won.

1148
00:37:14,579 --> 00:37:15,578
[10,000 won...!]
10,000 won?

1149
00:37:15,579 --> 00:37:16,645
But you're not gonna buy it.

1150
00:37:16,646 --> 00:37:17,978
(Shakes head)
Nope, nope.

1151
00:37:19,478 --> 00:37:20,945
[Firm]
It doesn't fit my personal color.

1152
00:37:21,045 --> 00:37:22,645
Then, that one…

1153
00:37:22,646 --> 00:37:24,578
[The prince’s offer]
Then, let's do it like this.

1154
00:37:24,678 --> 00:37:25,645
When it doesn’t sell,

1155
00:37:25,646 --> 00:37:27,678
pull a "The boss has gone mad" mega sale.

1156
00:37:27,679 --> 00:37:29,278
[Instantly on board]
The boss has gone mad!

1157
00:37:29,279 --> 00:37:30,245
Then, I'll…

1158
00:37:30,645 --> 00:37:32,411
Oh…but this cracked…

1159
00:37:32,419 --> 00:37:34,552
- I was hoping you'd buy it.
- Oh, really?

1160
00:37:34,678 --> 00:37:36,278
Why would you
want me to buy a broken item…

1161
00:37:36,279 --> 00:37:37,895
[Because the story behind it matters...]
It’s got an engraving and all.

1162
00:37:37,896 --> 00:37:38,811
Oh, because of the story behind it.

1163
00:37:38,812 --> 00:37:41,145
But keeping broken stuff at home
messes with your feng shui.

1164
00:37:41,146 --> 00:37:41,911
Oh, right, right!

1165
00:37:42,078 --> 00:37:43,369
[The Chicago guy knows his feng shui]

1166
00:37:43,370 --> 00:37:45,477
- It even has his name engraved on it.
- Yeah, yeah.

1167
00:37:45,478 --> 00:37:47,778
They say if your phone screen cracks,
you gotta change it ASAP!

1168
00:37:47,779 --> 00:37:49,178
True, having a broken mirror at home
makes your luck go away.

1169
00:37:49,179 --> 00:37:51,478
Yeah, it said your luck goes away.

1170
00:37:51,981 --> 00:37:52,779
[Egyptian Traditional Outfit]
One, two, three items!

1171
00:37:52,780 --> 00:37:53,670
[Cleopatra Stone Slab]
Then, for these three,

1172
00:37:53,678 --> 00:37:54,695
[Egyptian Beer]
2,500 pounds.

1173
00:37:54,696 --> 00:37:55,878
[A bundle deal for 2,500 pounds]
2,500 pounds.

1174
00:37:55,879 --> 00:37:57,188
[Hmm...]
2,500 would be…

1175
00:37:57,189 --> 00:37:58,611
Around 75,000 won?

1176
00:37:58,612 --> 00:38:00,076
- That's quite pricey!
- Then…

1177
00:38:00,077 --> 00:38:01,212
Why does it feel like
it just got even more expensive??

1178
00:38:01,212 --> 00:38:02,778
[Giving up]
I’m done, that’s it for me!

1179
00:38:02,779 --> 00:38:03,778
Then…

1180
00:38:03,779 --> 00:38:04,778
[Discounted price: 2,000 pounds]
2,000 pounds.

1181
00:38:04,779 --> 00:38:05,878
2,000 pounds,
about 60,000 won.

1182
00:38:05,879 --> 00:38:06,678
60,000 won.

1183
00:38:06,812 --> 00:38:08,345
The beer must be really pricey.

1184
00:38:08,346 --> 00:38:10,145
[So how much is it?]
Yeah, how much is the beer?

1185
00:38:10,378 --> 00:38:11,778
- The beer was a bit expensive.
- Oh, really?

1186
00:38:11,878 --> 00:38:13,945
Because it’s hard
to find alcohol around here.

1187
00:38:14,378 --> 00:38:16,245
The beer's only 1,500 won each?

1188
00:38:16,378 --> 00:38:17,678
YOHAN's buying it for me!

1189
00:38:18,078 --> 00:38:20,311
[About 6,000 won]
[Bought 4 beers for 200 pounds]

1190
00:38:20,378 --> 00:38:21,878
[Egyptian Beer buying price: 200 pounds]
But yeah, there really aren’t many places selling alcohol.

1191
00:38:21,879 --> 00:38:23,545
[Justifying the high price through scarcity marketing]
There was literally only one spot that did.

1192
00:38:23,645 --> 00:38:26,078
Like, if there had been 3 cans of beer,

1193
00:38:26,079 --> 00:38:27,911
It probably would’ve
looked way more legit.

1194
00:38:27,912 --> 00:38:30,111
- He drank two cans himself.
- Yeah, so there's only one can left.

1195
00:38:30,112 --> 00:38:31,578
But!

1196
00:38:31,579 --> 00:38:33,345
We drank it together.

1197
00:38:33,745 --> 00:38:36,145
[The paupers' beer party last night]
This is SHINDONG's.

1198
00:38:36,146 --> 00:38:37,445
Tomorrow!

1199
00:38:37,778 --> 00:38:38,778
[Self-consumed while wishing to become a prince]
To become princes!

1200
00:38:38,779 --> 00:38:41,378
I wanna be a prince!

1201
00:38:41,778 --> 00:38:42,545
We got it, for now.

1202
00:38:42,546 --> 00:38:44,178
[YOHAN’s items are on hold]
We'll think it over.

1203
00:38:44,179 --> 00:38:45,545
I really gotta think this through.

1204
00:38:45,546 --> 00:38:46,811
[Second sale: Merchant JISUNG]
Merchant JISUNG.

1205
00:38:46,812 --> 00:38:47,278
[Clap!]

1206
00:38:47,279 --> 00:38:47,778
Ha!

1207
00:38:47,945 --> 00:38:49,511
- Yes!
- Two necklaces.

1208
00:38:49,512 --> 00:38:50,244
[Entering with a lot of hype]
Whoo!

1209
00:38:50,245 --> 00:38:52,211
I think he has to sell
the necklaces at a high price.

1210
00:38:52,511 --> 00:38:53,178
[Clap!]

1211
00:38:53,179 --> 00:38:54,011
That one!

1212
00:38:54,079 --> 00:38:55,845
That's a real gem!

1213
00:38:55,978 --> 00:38:57,845
But seriously,
opals are quite expensive.

1214
00:38:57,846 --> 00:38:59,111
Yes, they're really expensive.

1215
00:38:59,112 --> 00:39:01,011
[Oh, really?]
Oh, they're usually expensive?

1216
00:39:01,211 --> 00:39:03,378
- It's a natural stone.
- This must be around 90,000 won.

1217
00:39:03,545 --> 00:39:04,945
First, it doesn't have any poison.

1218
00:39:04,946 --> 00:39:06,778
And it's one of a kind in the world...

1219
00:39:06,779 --> 00:39:08,078
Seriously, this is…

1220
00:39:08,211 --> 00:39:09,510
This is one of a kind…

1221
00:39:09,511 --> 00:39:11,444
Aren't there different variations
of the same thing?

1222
00:39:11,445 --> 00:39:12,578
This is the only one with color!

1223
00:39:12,579 --> 00:39:14,578
But I realized this
after seeing it.

1224
00:39:14,579 --> 00:39:16,081
I don't think I'm a fan of opal.

1225
00:39:16,082 --> 00:39:18,078
- Oh, you don't really want it.
- Yeah.

1226
00:39:18,145 --> 00:39:20,311
- Everyone's got their own thing that they like.
- Yes.

1227
00:39:20,678 --> 00:39:22,311
[Swoosh]
But it is pretty.

1228
00:39:22,378 --> 00:39:23,478
It kind of has
a Tiffany & Co. vibe.

1229
00:39:23,479 --> 00:39:24,645
[Snap!]
That’s right, that’s right.

1230
00:39:24,811 --> 00:39:26,711
Huh? But…

1231
00:39:26,878 --> 00:39:28,078
- Oh, wait.
- Huh?

1232
00:39:28,079 --> 00:39:29,345
There's another one
exactly like this!

1233
00:39:29,346 --> 00:39:30,911
- Hey, there's a lot!
- Huh?

1234
00:39:30,945 --> 00:39:32,211
I... I

1235
00:39:32,311 --> 00:39:34,445
[More "one-of-a-kind" items than expected]
The same kind of thing…

1236
00:39:34,645 --> 00:39:35,967
[Urgent]
I actually uploaded that earlier!

1237
00:39:35,974 --> 00:39:36,984
[Shameless]
Yeah, I uploaded that earlier.

1238
00:39:36,985 --> 00:39:39,351
[The Gen Z merchant even sells online]
Oh, you even sell online?

1239
00:39:39,445 --> 00:39:40,978
How much?
Let's check the price.

1240
00:39:40,979 --> 00:39:41,878
(Nervous)
I'll check the price.

1241
00:39:41,879 --> 00:39:43,811
Wait…
You can't…use the phone.

1242
00:39:43,812 --> 00:39:44,778
(Can’t hear)

1243
00:39:44,958 --> 00:39:46,111
- Oh, because this…
- It's ch…cheating…

1244
00:39:46,112 --> 00:39:48,478
- The person buying has to check carefully before buying.
- That's right, that's right.

1245
00:39:48,945 --> 00:39:50,977
[Anxious...]
UK... No, wait.

1246
00:39:50,978 --> 00:39:52,178
(Looking up the Korean price)
I think this is that.

1247
00:39:52,179 --> 00:39:53,345
121 lira?

1248
00:39:53,346 --> 00:39:55,345
But I’m really curious
how much it actually costs.

1249
00:39:55,346 --> 00:39:56,778
[So curious]
I'm curious. I'm also very curious.

1250
00:39:56,779 --> 00:39:58,178
[Curious here too]
It was pretty expensive.

1251
00:39:58,445 --> 00:39:59,978
In Korean won.

1252
00:39:59,979 --> 00:40:01,011
- In Korean won?
- Yeah.

1253
00:40:01,145 --> 00:40:01,845
[ctrl+c]
Republic of Korea.

1254
00:40:01,846 --> 00:40:03,245
[ctrl+v]
Republic of Korea.

1255
00:40:03,246 --> 00:40:04,811
He's really bad
at using the cellphone!

1256
00:40:06,611 --> 00:40:07,711
- Oh, here it is!
- Yeah.

1257
00:40:07,911 --> 00:40:09,011
Huh?

1258
00:40:09,012 --> 00:40:10,045
240,000 won.

1259
00:40:10,046 --> 00:40:11,611
- Oh, it's still quite pricey.
- Yeah.

1260
00:40:11,862 --> 00:40:13,178
[Nice]
It's expensive, it's expensive.

1261
00:40:13,571 --> 00:40:14,245
It's pricey.

1262
00:40:14,246 --> 00:40:15,462
Was that person an angel?

1263
00:40:15,463 --> 00:40:16,311
"Was that person an angel"…

1264
00:40:16,312 --> 00:40:17,975
[Dummy]
Don't say things like that! Don't say it!

1265
00:40:17,976 --> 00:40:19,278
No, so this is

1266
00:40:19,578 --> 00:40:22,478
- what's being sold at a store!
- Right, because it's now being distributed.

1267
00:40:22,478 --> 00:40:23,865
So 240,000 won?

1268
00:40:23,866 --> 00:40:26,478
- But I did bargain.
- How much after the discount?

1269
00:40:26,678 --> 00:40:27,578
[Snap]

1270
00:40:27,579 --> 00:40:28,678
[Opal necklace]
120,000 won.

1271
00:40:28,679 --> 00:40:30,077
[Selling price: Around 4,000 pounds]
120,000 won.

1272
00:40:30,078 --> 00:40:32,545
- Wow, you cut it down a lot!
- You got a big discount!

1273
00:40:32,945 --> 00:40:34,678
It does look like DAWN's style.

1274
00:40:34,679 --> 00:40:36,145
- This?
- It's not? It's not?

1275
00:40:36,146 --> 00:40:37,777
[Quick appeal]
I think it really suits

1276
00:40:37,778 --> 00:40:39,545
[Sniff, sniff]
someone sexy.

1277
00:40:39,546 --> 00:40:40,877
It really is pretty.

1278
00:40:40,878 --> 00:40:42,245
Oh, but it's way too expensive.

1279
00:40:42,246 --> 00:40:43,978
How much were you thinking?

1280
00:40:43,979 --> 00:40:45,278
Me? How much?

1281
00:40:45,845 --> 00:40:46,577
Oh…

1282
00:40:46,578 --> 00:40:48,078
[Opal Necklace selling price: Around 4,000 pounds]
(120,000 won)

1283
00:40:48,079 --> 00:40:49,278
About…

1284
00:40:52,079 --> 00:40:53,211
600 pounds…?

1285
00:40:53,875 --> 00:40:54,878
- 600 pounds?
- 18,000 won?

1286
00:40:54,879 --> 00:40:56,545
[Opal necklace selling price: Around 4,000 pounds]
600 pounds.

1287
00:40:56,546 --> 00:40:57,678
27,000 won.

1288
00:40:57,679 --> 00:40:59,878
[Offer price: -85%]
Oh, 600 pounds…

1289
00:40:59,879 --> 00:41:01,711
[600 pounds: About 18,000 won]
That’s only 18,000 won.

1290
00:41:02,111 --> 00:41:03,711
I know some

1291
00:41:03,712 --> 00:41:07,845
professional vendors
in the Jongno area.

1292
00:41:08,045 --> 00:41:09,645
They give me really good deals.

1293
00:41:09,646 --> 00:41:11,078
Oh…

1294
00:41:11,079 --> 00:41:14,046
[A prince with industry connections]
It honestly doesn't give me much of an incentive.

1295
00:41:14,046 --> 00:41:16,111
- Since he knows the market price.
- Since he knows it!

1296
00:41:16,112 --> 00:41:18,311
[Unexpected insider info]
Someone you know will give you a better deal.

1297
00:41:18,312 --> 00:41:20,111
Just put it down...

1298
00:41:20,778 --> 00:41:22,111
JISUNG…

1299
00:41:22,178 --> 00:41:25,111
You've been rubbing
your hands a lot since yesterday.

1300
00:41:25,445 --> 00:41:27,478
[His hands got busy
whenever he was in trouble]

1301
00:41:27,479 --> 00:41:30,278
[Very transparent
about his mental state]

1302
00:41:30,478 --> 00:41:31,878
(Made another appearance today)

1303
00:41:32,145 --> 00:41:33,778
Please think over
my offer of 600 pounds.

1304
00:41:33,845 --> 00:41:35,078
[You want me to think about -85%?]
Uh…

1305
00:41:35,079 --> 00:41:36,878
I’ll… think it over, yeah.

1306
00:41:36,978 --> 00:41:39,211
[Third sale: Merchant SHINDONG]
Alright, everyone, let’s go.

1307
00:41:39,545 --> 00:41:41,811
I have to think
of myself as a tourist!

1308
00:41:42,078 --> 00:41:44,445
[Picking souvenirs from a tourist’s POV]
The magnets are pretty.

1309
00:41:44,446 --> 00:41:46,378
Oh, good!

1310
00:41:46,478 --> 00:41:48,178
[Winning them over with variety!]
Oh, nice!

1311
00:41:48,179 --> 00:41:50,078
Oh, this is pretty!

1312
00:41:50,345 --> 00:41:53,078
[As many as 14 items,
including freebies]

1313
00:41:53,211 --> 00:41:55,245
I decided to buy
several inexpensive souvenirs

1314
00:41:55,246 --> 00:41:57,345
that would remind them
of this place,

1315
00:41:57,545 --> 00:41:59,778
[Strategist SHINDONG’s choice]
so I could still make a good profit even if I didn’t sell them all.

1316
00:41:59,779 --> 00:42:01,145
[Diversifying investments rather than going all-in]
That was my thought process.

1317
00:42:01,278 --> 00:42:04,078
[Starting lightly with the magnets]
Let's first start with each of these.

1318
00:42:04,079 --> 00:42:05,978
I'll give it to you for cheap!
5 dollars!

1319
00:42:06,078 --> 00:42:07,267
[Three types of magnets]
5 dollars each!

1320
00:42:07,268 --> 00:42:08,288
[Selling price: 250 pounds each]
5 dollars?

1321
00:42:08,289 --> 00:42:09,245
(About 7,500 won)
Just an easy 5 dollars.

1322
00:42:09,246 --> 00:42:09,845
7,500 won.

1323
00:42:09,846 --> 00:42:10,945
For one?
Or for all three?

1324
00:42:10,946 --> 00:42:11,778
For one!

1325
00:42:11,779 --> 00:42:13,011
Yeah, you have to
buy them one by one.

1326
00:42:13,012 --> 00:42:14,911
Come on!
Just give it to me for 5,000 won.

1327
00:42:15,078 --> 00:42:16,511
But 5,000 won is
actually a bit pricey.

1328
00:42:16,678 --> 00:42:18,178
5,000 won is pricey?

1329
00:42:18,179 --> 00:42:19,411
Have you never
bought magnets before?

1330
00:42:19,412 --> 00:42:20,178
[Nope]
I haven't.

1331
00:42:20,179 --> 00:42:21,685
How can 5,000 won be expensive?

1332
00:42:21,686 --> 00:42:23,585
[First time showing interest]
I’ll take 2 for 10,000 won.

1333
00:42:23,586 --> 00:42:24,678
- 2 for 10,000 won?
- Yes.

1334
00:42:24,679 --> 00:42:26,311
(Thinking)
2 for 10,000 won?

1335
00:42:26,312 --> 00:42:27,345
- Okay.
- 3 for 10,000 won!

1336
00:42:27,346 --> 00:42:28,211
It’d be awkward
for the last one left over.

1337
00:42:28,212 --> 00:42:29,778
3 for 10,000 won is way too cheap.

1338
00:42:29,779 --> 00:42:32,211
- I’m basically selling at a loss.
- Oh, really?

1339
00:42:32,378 --> 00:42:34,005
[Magnet / Magnet / Magnet]
I’ll give you 3 for 13,000 won!

1340
00:42:34,006 --> 00:42:36,378
[Bundle selling price: Around 433 pounds]
Oh, 3,000 won? I want it nice and even.

1341
00:42:36,379 --> 00:42:37,978
- 2 for 10,000 won.
- 2 for 10,000 won.

1342
00:42:37,979 --> 00:42:39,278
2 for 10,000 won,
3 for 13,000 won.

1343
00:42:39,279 --> 00:42:40,478
Which would you like?

1344
00:42:40,479 --> 00:42:41,978
He sure is good at this.

1345
00:42:41,979 --> 00:42:43,578
[Persistent]
3 for 11,000 won.

1346
00:42:43,579 --> 00:42:45,082
[Rejection]
No, but 11,000 won is too little…

1347
00:42:45,083 --> 00:42:46,468
- 3 for 11,000 won.
- 11,000 won is a no-go.

1348
00:42:46,469 --> 00:42:48,511
- 3 for 11,500 won.
- Oh, nope, no way.

1349
00:42:48,512 --> 00:42:49,378
- I'm not selling to this person.
- 12,000 won!

1350
00:42:49,379 --> 00:42:51,110
[Not selling to you]
No, I'm not selling! I'm not selling to this person!

1351
00:42:51,111 --> 00:42:51,978
[Upset]
You won't take 12,000 won?

1352
00:42:51,979 --> 00:42:52,911
I won’t, I won’t, yeah.

1353
00:42:52,912 --> 00:42:55,445
[Re-approaching the first bidder]
2 for 10,000 won, 3 for 13,000 won.

1354
00:42:55,446 --> 00:42:56,678
[No change: 2 for 10,000 won]
I’ll do 2 for 10,000 won.

1355
00:42:56,679 --> 00:42:57,711
2 for 10,000 won!
Which ones will you choose?

1356
00:42:57,712 --> 00:42:58,698
- I’ll take these 2.
- Okay!

1357
00:42:58,699 --> 00:43:00,491
[Sold]
Wow, you bought it right away.

1358
00:43:00,492 --> 00:43:02,993
- But since he picked first.
- You're already buying?

1359
00:43:02,994 --> 00:43:05,010
[A smooth deal! Today's first purchase]
10,000 won! 2 for 10,000 won.

1360
00:43:05,011 --> 00:43:05,878
Only one left!

1361
00:43:05,879 --> 00:43:07,378
Hey, this is pretty.
I want to buy this.

1362
00:43:07,379 --> 00:43:07,945
How much?

1363
00:43:07,946 --> 00:43:09,677
Clearance sale?

1364
00:43:09,678 --> 00:43:10,978
- Clearance sale…?
- Clearance sale!

1365
00:43:10,979 --> 00:43:11,545
How can this be a clearance sale?

1366
00:43:11,546 --> 00:43:13,345
[Clearance frenzy]
Clearance, clearance, clearance, clearance!

1367
00:43:13,346 --> 00:43:14,378
This person

1368
00:43:14,379 --> 00:43:15,945
just bought 2 for 10,000 won.

1369
00:43:15,946 --> 00:43:17,311
I can't sell it for
anything less than that!

1370
00:43:17,312 --> 00:43:18,711
No, since there's one left!

1371
00:43:18,712 --> 00:43:20,211
- A quick sale.
- No, no.

1372
00:43:20,212 --> 00:43:21,378
- A quick sale.
- I'm not selling.

1373
00:43:21,379 --> 00:43:22,445
Oh, wait, wait!

1374
00:43:22,446 --> 00:43:23,778
How much are you thinking then?

1375
00:43:23,779 --> 00:43:25,045
Because he bought
2 for 10,000 won.

1376
00:43:25,046 --> 00:43:26,545
You have to pay
at least 5,000 won.

1377
00:43:26,546 --> 00:43:28,945
No, you have to get
rid of the one left…

1378
00:43:28,946 --> 00:43:29,711
I'm not selling.

1379
00:43:29,712 --> 00:43:30,411
3,000 won!

1380
00:43:30,412 --> 00:43:31,345
[NO]
No way! Then…

1381
00:43:31,346 --> 00:43:32,545
Then, I would have
just given it to him!

1382
00:43:32,546 --> 00:43:33,545
No.

1383
00:43:33,546 --> 00:43:34,745
If you just gave it to him,
then you wouldn't get 3,000 won.

1384
00:43:34,746 --> 00:43:35,945
If you give it to me,
you will get 3,000 won.

1385
00:43:35,946 --> 00:43:37,312
Then he might not have bought it.

1386
00:43:37,312 --> 00:43:38,278
But he already bought it!

1387
00:43:38,279 --> 00:43:39,511
Did you buy it?
Is it a done deal?

1388
00:43:39,512 --> 00:43:40,711
Yes, I'm done.

1389
00:43:40,878 --> 00:43:42,778
- 3,000 won.
- Wait, hold up!

1390
00:43:42,779 --> 00:43:43,911
2,000 won.

1391
00:43:43,912 --> 00:43:45,183
It's basically a clearance sale!

1392
00:43:45,184 --> 00:43:46,445
[A smooth negotiator]

1393
00:43:46,446 --> 00:43:48,245
[Bargaining once again]
2,000 won, 2,000 won!

1394
00:43:48,246 --> 00:43:49,978
But, honestly…

1395
00:43:49,979 --> 00:43:51,778
- No, no.
- Why not?

1396
00:43:51,779 --> 00:43:53,378
How much is 2,000 won?

1397
00:43:53,379 --> 00:43:54,778
It's not even 1 dollar!

1398
00:43:54,878 --> 00:43:56,378
- DAWN's not even thinking about buying it.
- No.

1399
00:43:56,379 --> 00:43:57,778
Otherwise,
it's just gonna get thrown away!

1400
00:43:57,779 --> 00:43:59,745
Do you want it to be trash,
or do you want to sell it for 1,000 won?

1401
00:43:59,746 --> 00:44:01,678
[Knocked off another 1,000 won]
Wait, right now…

1402
00:44:01,679 --> 00:44:03,878
I paid 5,000 won for one of these!

1403
00:44:03,879 --> 00:44:05,778
Then, I'll just take it instead.

1404
00:44:05,778 --> 00:44:06,678
3,000 won?

1405
00:44:06,679 --> 00:44:07,511
Let’s settle for 1,500 won.

1406
00:44:07,738 --> 00:44:08,671
[What are you saying...?]
What are you even talking about?

1407
00:44:08,679 --> 00:44:09,878
[1,000 won / 3,000 won]
I want 1,000 won, you want 3,000 won.

1408
00:44:09,879 --> 00:44:11,045
[1,500 won]
So let’s meet in the middle at 1,500 won.

1409
00:44:11,046 --> 00:44:12,668
What's with this guy?
I'm not selling!

1410
00:44:12,669 --> 00:44:13,345
Oh, wait a sec!

1411
00:44:13,346 --> 00:44:14,345
3,000 won! 3,000 won!

1412
00:44:14,346 --> 00:44:15,145
You can't sell it for 2,000 won?

1413
00:44:15,146 --> 00:44:17,381
We're moving on
to the next item, everyone!

1414
00:44:17,382 --> 00:44:18,611
It glows in the dark!

1415
00:44:18,612 --> 00:44:20,578
[3 types of glow-in-the-dark papyrus art]
It glows in the dark, everyone!

1416
00:44:20,678 --> 00:44:22,345
It'd be perfect
in a home with kids!

1417
00:44:22,346 --> 00:44:23,411
[Papyrus Art selling price: 1,000 pounds each]
It's 30,000 won each.

1418
00:44:23,412 --> 00:44:24,745
(One piece /30,000 won)
[Silence...]

1419
00:44:24,911 --> 00:44:26,345
[Strong preferences]
Not me.

1420
00:44:26,411 --> 00:44:28,978
I bought three,
so each person can get one!

1421
00:44:30,337 --> 00:44:31,875
Oh…I'm starting to soften up…

1422
00:44:31,876 --> 00:44:32,778
No, no!

1423
00:44:32,779 --> 00:44:34,511
- I was thinking of all of you…
- I'm curious about the price of this one.

1424
00:44:34,512 --> 00:44:36,678
I thought about JOHNNY,
who's long and lean,

1425
00:44:36,679 --> 00:44:38,611
- and picked this one.
- Oh, really? What about this one?

1426
00:44:38,612 --> 00:44:41,078
[Smooth talker]
This is LEETEUK, the angel with wings!

1427
00:44:41,085 --> 00:44:42,417
- Oh, is that so?
- Yes.

1428
00:44:42,545 --> 00:44:43,545
- What about this one?
- And…

1429
00:44:43,745 --> 00:44:45,111
Anyone can tell that's DAWN!

1430
00:44:45,245 --> 00:44:47,511
[Finale]
"DAWN" as in "Shoot it down there!"

1431
00:44:47,512 --> 00:44:48,578
[Explanation sealed with confidence]
It's DAWN, DAWN!

1432
00:44:48,579 --> 00:44:49,945
- Wow!
- DAWN!

1433
00:44:49,946 --> 00:44:51,152
You nailed it.

1434
00:44:51,153 --> 00:44:52,311
It's definitely DAWN.

1435
00:44:52,312 --> 00:44:53,982
[Touched]
Wow, seriously!

1436
00:44:53,983 --> 00:44:56,078
Back in the day, you know
those inventors selling their gadgets

1437
00:44:56,079 --> 00:44:57,845
would sometimes visit schools

1438
00:44:57,991 --> 00:45:00,658
[Curiosity overload]
and suddenly start up the power trimmers,

1439
00:45:00,679 --> 00:45:02,511
[A demo that grabs your eye]
and they'd start buzzing and cutting,

1440
00:45:02,512 --> 00:45:05,411
and the kids would go absolutely wild?

1441
00:45:05,578 --> 00:45:07,611
When SHINDONG starts talking,

1442
00:45:07,612 --> 00:45:09,711
it takes me back to my childhood.

1443
00:45:10,211 --> 00:45:12,844
[A master merchant is a master merchant]
There’s a reason SHINDONG does so much business.

1444
00:45:13,179 --> 00:45:15,478
[Encore]
Whether the horse jumps up or comes down,

1445
00:45:15,479 --> 00:45:16,345
- it's still DAWN!
- He's such a businessman!

1446
00:45:16,346 --> 00:45:18,078
This one is DAWN's.

1447
00:45:18,079 --> 00:45:20,678
[Just handing it over first]
The slim and sleek one is JOHNNY's.

1448
00:45:20,778 --> 00:45:23,578
[The princes take it as if enchanted]
The wingless angel is LEETEUK's.

1449
00:45:23,579 --> 00:45:25,045
I'll offer an unprecedented price!

1450
00:45:25,046 --> 00:45:26,211
You can have it
for the original price.

1451
00:45:26,278 --> 00:45:27,711
[Papyrus Art discount price: Around 666 pounds]
Let's go with 20,000 won each. 20,000 won!

1452
00:45:27,712 --> 00:45:29,011
(One piece/20,000 won)
What's the original price per piece?

1453
00:45:29,012 --> 00:45:30,311
- 20,000 won. I paid 20,000 won for it.
- For real?

1454
00:45:30,312 --> 00:45:32,581
[Slowly getting captivated by his words]
Wow, you’re such a smooth talker.

1455
00:45:32,582 --> 00:45:34,574
[He gives no room to think and moves onto the next item]
Honestly, this is the main item!

1456
00:45:34,574 --> 00:45:35,674
- This is the main item.
- That's right, yes.

1457
00:45:35,675 --> 00:45:37,295
[3 types of pyramids]
You have to buy this one.

1458
00:45:37,296 --> 00:45:38,345
This is just…

1459
00:45:38,346 --> 00:45:41,511
[Naturally handed each of them over]
You have to take it. There's no way around it!

1460
00:45:41,778 --> 00:45:42,778
How much is this?

1461
00:45:42,779 --> 00:45:45,062
[Pyramid selling price: About 1,000 pounds]
It’s 30,000 won each, 30,000 won each!

1462
00:45:45,063 --> 00:45:45,645
(One piece/30,000 won)
30,000 won?

1463
00:45:45,646 --> 00:45:47,345
So altogether,
it's like 50,000 won?

1464
00:45:47,345 --> 00:45:48,709
50,000 won, that’s right.

1465
00:45:48,711 --> 00:45:50,611
[Bundle price: About 1,333 pounds]
If you take both items, I'll give them to you for 40,000 won!

1466
00:45:50,612 --> 00:45:51,978
- Wow!
- 40,000 won.

1467
00:45:51,979 --> 00:45:52,978
This and this for 40,000 won.

1468
00:45:52,979 --> 00:45:53,678
This for 40,000 won.

1469
00:45:53,679 --> 00:45:55,245
Why did I say "Wow"?

1470
00:45:55,246 --> 00:45:56,878
[Pyramid]
If I just buy this, how much would it be?

1471
00:45:56,879 --> 00:45:57,978
[Single item]
Then it’s 30,000 won.

1472
00:45:57,979 --> 00:45:58,978
[No discount on singles]
No discounts on that one.

1473
00:45:58,979 --> 00:46:00,878
There's no discount
if you only buy one.

1474
00:46:01,238 --> 00:46:03,371
If you buy 2, it's 40,000 won.
But if it's just 1, then it's 30,000 won.

1475
00:46:03,379 --> 00:46:04,881
If it were me, I’d buy 2.

1476
00:46:04,882 --> 00:46:06,078
You have to buy this one.

1477
00:46:06,245 --> 00:46:07,878
- He…He's good.
- I know, right?

1478
00:46:07,879 --> 00:46:09,378
I just can't argue with that…

1479
00:46:09,379 --> 00:46:11,445
And now, the last one remaining!

1480
00:46:11,545 --> 00:46:14,411
[Anubis statue]
Okay, this one…! It's a bit awkward to talk about.

1481
00:46:14,611 --> 00:46:16,911
I was originally
gonna pick the cat,

1482
00:46:16,912 --> 00:46:18,645
but then I heard
DAWN has a dog…!

1483
00:46:18,646 --> 00:46:21,477
[Tailored for DAWN’s preference]
So for our furry friends, this is a must-have.

1484
00:46:21,578 --> 00:46:22,878
I hustled and bargained hard,

1485
00:46:22,879 --> 00:46:24,545
and ended up
buying it for 1,500 pounds.

1486
00:46:24,611 --> 00:46:25,778
I'll cut you a deal!

1487
00:46:25,779 --> 00:46:27,245
[Anubis Statue selling price: Around 1,000 pounds]
I’ll let you have it for 30,000 won, too.

1488
00:46:27,378 --> 00:46:29,844
[The master merchant doesn't give them a chance to speak]
And then you have to take these things in a bag!

1489
00:46:29,845 --> 00:46:32,278
[A set of 3 Egypt eco bags]
Yes, this…! This is…!

1490
00:46:32,279 --> 00:46:33,545
I kind of want this one.

1491
00:46:33,546 --> 00:46:34,978
[Eco Bag discounted price: Around 166 pounds]
I'll give it to you just for 5,000 won.

1492
00:46:34,979 --> 00:46:36,045
(1 bag/5,000 won)
I'll give it to you for 5,000 won each.

1493
00:46:36,046 --> 00:46:37,278
- One for 5,000 won?
- Yes, 5,000 won!

1494
00:46:37,279 --> 00:46:38,478
[If you buy something else]
But only if you buy this!

1495
00:46:38,479 --> 00:46:39,478
What if I don't?

1496
00:46:39,479 --> 00:46:41,076
[Single item price: About 333 pounds]
If you don't buy it, then 10,000 won. I bought it for 10,000 won.

1497
00:46:41,077 --> 00:46:42,611
- That's so expensive!
- No.

1498
00:46:42,612 --> 00:46:44,878
You can't get this in Korea!
It's only in Egypt!

1499
00:46:44,978 --> 00:46:47,411
I should be charging
way more, to be honest...

1500
00:46:47,412 --> 00:46:49,578
[Pyramid / Eco bag]
For this and a bag…!

1501
00:46:49,579 --> 00:46:51,678
[Purchase price: About 933 pounds]
If you sell it to me for 28,000 won,

1502
00:46:51,679 --> 00:46:52,811
[Big spender]
I’ll buy it right now!

1503
00:46:52,812 --> 00:46:54,545
28,000 won means
you gotta include that one too!

1504
00:46:54,678 --> 00:46:55,778
[Two for 10,000 won]
Oh, this, the price we mentioned earlier.

1505
00:46:55,779 --> 00:46:56,744
[Already decided on buying the magnet set]
Oh, 10,000 won.

1506
00:46:56,745 --> 00:46:57,578
He's good at buying.

1507
00:46:57,579 --> 00:46:58,878
- It's 38,000 won.
- Okay, okay.

1508
00:46:58,879 --> 00:47:00,545
[SOLD OUT]
This is a deal! Yes, it's a deal!

1509
00:47:00,546 --> 00:47:02,611
[Buying right away]
I'll also buy that set.

1510
00:47:02,612 --> 00:47:03,180
Wow…!

1511
00:47:03,181 --> 00:47:05,011
Since he already offered 28,000 won,

1512
00:47:05,012 --> 00:47:07,545
[SOLD OUT]
28,000 won for you! Okay! 28,000 won!

1513
00:47:07,546 --> 00:47:08,711
JOHNNY, you don't need this one?

1514
00:47:08,719 --> 00:47:11,385
[A customized trade for cat-faced JOHNNY]
You can switch, if you'd like.

1515
00:47:11,478 --> 00:47:13,178
Then what image is left now?

1516
00:47:13,179 --> 00:47:14,611
[The last remaining eco bag]
I have this image left.

1517
00:47:14,612 --> 00:47:15,545
Nothing else?

1518
00:47:15,546 --> 00:47:16,178
Of course, there are!

1519
00:47:16,179 --> 00:47:16,911
What other things do you have?

1520
00:47:16,912 --> 00:47:17,678
Here you go!

1521
00:47:18,345 --> 00:47:19,011
[The design flipped upside down]

1522
00:47:19,012 --> 00:47:20,171
[The design on the other side]

1523
00:47:20,172 --> 00:47:21,278
No, like…

1524
00:47:21,279 --> 00:47:22,311
This is just a leftover, right?

1525
00:47:22,378 --> 00:47:23,981
[The clearance sale strategy returns]
What do you mean by "leftover"? Not yet…

1526
00:47:23,982 --> 00:47:25,378
- LEETEUK, what's with you?
- Clearance, clearance, clearance.

1527
00:47:25,379 --> 00:47:26,188
- Clearance?
- Oh, this guy…!

1528
00:47:26,189 --> 00:47:27,811
- He only likes clearances!
- Clearance, clearance, clearance!

1529
00:47:27,812 --> 00:47:29,478
This guy only likes clearances!
What are we gonna do?

1530
00:47:29,479 --> 00:47:31,778
When you go to the supermarket
right before closing,

1531
00:47:31,779 --> 00:47:34,045
the staff there says,
"Just take it."

1532
00:47:34,096 --> 00:47:35,777
[Pyramid]
LEETEUK, you have to take this one.

1533
00:47:35,778 --> 00:47:36,392
Right?

1534
00:47:36,393 --> 00:47:38,378
[Pyramid]
So, let me see it. The one with my name.

1535
00:47:38,379 --> 00:47:39,345
[Magnet]
And this too.

1536
00:47:39,346 --> 00:47:40,378
- This and…
- And?

1537
00:47:40,379 --> 00:47:41,371
[Eco bag]
And this too!

1538
00:47:41,372 --> 00:47:42,480
With all of those?

1539
00:47:42,481 --> 00:47:44,045
[Bundle price: About 666 pounds]
Uh, how about 20,000 won for everything?

1540
00:47:44,046 --> 00:47:46,045
What are you saying?
They bought them all for 28,000 won!

1541
00:47:46,046 --> 00:47:47,578
- It's a clearance sale, right?
- I'll give it to you for 30,000 won!

1542
00:47:47,579 --> 00:47:48,645
A mega sale!

1543
00:47:48,646 --> 00:47:50,877
- A mega sale is usually 50% off…
- I'll give it to you for 30,000 won.

1544
00:47:50,878 --> 00:47:51,911
The sale even
goes to 80% off!

1545
00:47:51,912 --> 00:47:52,678
[The price negotiation gets tense]
It’s a clearance sale!

1546
00:47:52,679 --> 00:47:54,078
[I'm not selling to you]
It's not a clearance. Then, I'm not selling.

1547
00:47:54,079 --> 00:47:55,876
- You're not selling?
- I'm not selling to you. No sale!

1548
00:47:55,877 --> 00:47:56,796
- No sale?
- No sale!

1549
00:47:56,797 --> 00:47:58,368
[Fine, then]
That just won't work, then!

1550
00:47:58,368 --> 00:47:59,510
- I couldn't buy…!
- No, like…!

1551
00:47:59,511 --> 00:48:01,278
- LEETEUK!
- Yes?

1552
00:48:01,279 --> 00:48:02,486
[Feeling hurt]
We're members of the same group…

1553
00:48:02,487 --> 00:48:03,611
Oh, exactly.

1554
00:48:04,192 --> 00:48:05,277
We're members of the same group…

1555
00:48:05,278 --> 00:48:06,291
No. 25,000 won.

1556
00:48:06,292 --> 00:48:07,030
Just spend a little…

1557
00:48:07,031 --> 00:48:08,111
28,000 won is a bit much…

1558
00:48:08,112 --> 00:48:10,211
[Sealing the deal]
When we get back to Korea, a round of golf is on me.

1559
00:48:10,212 --> 00:48:11,178
[Secret weapon]

1560
00:48:11,179 --> 00:48:12,005
Oh, really?

1561
00:48:12,012 --> 00:48:12,945
[Intrigued]
Oh, really?

1562
00:48:12,945 --> 00:48:13,945
Really.

1563
00:48:13,945 --> 00:48:15,645
[More than the souvenirs]
Isn't golf pricier, though?

1564
00:48:15,646 --> 00:48:17,711
- I'll go with that! Just buy it for 30,000 won!
- Oh really?

1565
00:48:17,811 --> 00:48:18,978
- You'll really cover golf?
- Please just do it once!

1566
00:48:18,979 --> 00:48:20,276
- I'll really pay for it. Promise!
- You'll really pay for golf?

1567
00:48:20,277 --> 00:48:21,177
[Promise!]
Promise! Okay!

1568
00:48:21,178 --> 00:48:22,245
- Okay, okay!
- Here, 30,000, 30,000!

1569
00:48:22,246 --> 00:48:23,775
[SOLD OUT]
30,000 won, 30,000 won! Okay! Done!

1570
00:48:23,776 --> 00:48:24,801
[Bundle price: Around 1,000 pounds]
30,000 won, 30,000 won! Done!

1571
00:48:24,801 --> 00:48:26,078
[Bonus offer: One round of golf]
30,000 won, done!

1572
00:48:26,079 --> 00:48:26,978
Wow, this is insane.

1573
00:48:26,979 --> 00:48:28,074
[Anubis Statue]
No one's interested in this?

1574
00:48:28,074 --> 00:48:28,879
Oh, I don't want that one.

1575
00:48:28,879 --> 00:48:30,645
It's too expensive.

1576
00:48:30,878 --> 00:48:31,678
I'll give it to you
for 10,000 won.

1577
00:48:31,679 --> 00:48:33,180
[30,000/10,000 won]
10,000 won, all of a sudden?

1578
00:48:33,181 --> 00:48:34,378
[A sudden flash deal alert]
This was originally about 50,000 won.

1579
00:48:34,379 --> 00:48:34,895
Hold on a sec!

1580
00:48:34,896 --> 00:48:36,678
- Buy it for 10,000 won.
- This is a clearance deal!

1581
00:48:36,679 --> 00:48:37,387
(It's practically free)
This is 10,000 won.

1582
00:48:37,388 --> 00:48:38,868
[SOLD OUT]
Okay. I'll buy this then.

1583
00:48:38,869 --> 00:48:40,578
- 10,000 won!
- I'm done, I'm done, I'm done.

1584
00:48:40,590 --> 00:48:42,178
Honestly, I don't

1585
00:48:42,378 --> 00:48:44,445
usually open my wallet that easily,

1586
00:48:44,446 --> 00:48:46,345
(Not really into shopping)
because I'm not really into shopping.

1587
00:48:46,545 --> 00:48:47,678
But SHINDONG…

1588
00:48:47,679 --> 00:48:49,245
[Spellbound]
He was so good at selling things.

1589
00:48:49,471 --> 00:48:52,071
I spent way too much.

1590
00:48:52,145 --> 00:48:53,811
[The price strategy of a business genius]
First, I set the price super high.

1591
00:48:53,812 --> 00:48:55,411
[Start high]
Truth is...

1592
00:48:55,978 --> 00:48:58,278
[Magnet: $1 each (50 pounds)]
Each magnet costs a dollar.

1593
00:48:58,279 --> 00:48:59,911
[1 magnet: 1,500 won]
But I sold two for 10,000 won!

1594
00:48:59,912 --> 00:49:00,945
Isn’t that insane?

1595
00:49:00,946 --> 00:49:02,978
[Sales genius and master merchant, SHINDONG]
This is how you do business, everyone.

1596
00:49:02,979 --> 00:49:05,311
[Magnet (each): Sold at 3.3 times the purchase price]
Down, down, down!

1597
00:49:05,312 --> 00:49:08,311
[Pyramid + Eco Bag Set: Sold at 2.2 times the purchase price]
Okay, thank you!

1598
00:49:08,312 --> 00:49:11,245
[Anubis Statue: Sold at 0.67 times the purchase price]
No, no!

1599
00:49:11,246 --> 00:49:14,578
[Glow-in-the-dark papyrus (1 type) art: sale fail]
How much? Okay, okay.

1600
00:49:14,778 --> 00:49:16,845
Hey, I think I can sell this
for a pretty penny.

1601
00:49:16,878 --> 00:49:18,545
Wow…That's amazing.

1602
00:49:18,878 --> 00:49:20,045
I’m good with this.

1603
00:49:20,046 --> 00:49:21,045
I feel like I got first place.

1604
00:49:21,046 --> 00:49:22,511
- YOHAN, go ahead and quickly sell your stuff.
- He's good at selling.

1605
00:49:22,512 --> 00:49:25,045
[The scarab slab with a serious defect]
But honestly, if it wasn't broken…!

1606
00:49:25,046 --> 00:49:27,011
I really would've bought it
if it weren't broken!

1607
00:49:27,178 --> 00:49:30,278
[Opal necklace]
DAWN was a prime candidate for this accessory,

1608
00:49:30,279 --> 00:49:31,945
but he knows an opal vendor.

1609
00:49:31,946 --> 00:49:32,811
Oh…

1610
00:49:32,878 --> 00:49:34,678
[Curious]
Do you have a story for us, JISUNG?

1611
00:49:34,679 --> 00:49:35,978
- Have a seat and tell us.
- Yeah.

1612
00:49:35,979 --> 00:49:38,311
[A sale needs a good story]
Oh…

1613
00:49:38,878 --> 00:49:41,178
It was honestly
my type of necklace…

1614
00:49:41,378 --> 00:49:42,474
[Upset]
But it was being totally ignored...

1615
00:49:42,475 --> 00:49:44,389
It made me
want to sell it even more!

1616
00:49:44,390 --> 00:49:46,945
So, I went all out
trying to hype it up.

1617
00:49:46,946 --> 00:49:48,711
[Adding a dash of pity]
I even tried to get some sympathy points.

1618
00:49:49,111 --> 00:49:50,178
It all started yesterday…

1619
00:49:50,179 --> 00:49:51,678
- It all started…
- Yesterday,

1620
00:49:51,679 --> 00:49:54,678
it was actually
my first time haggling…

1621
00:49:54,679 --> 00:49:55,878
Oh, so you'd never haggled before.

1622
00:49:55,879 --> 00:49:58,111
It was my first time visiting
a market where bargaining is common.

1623
00:49:58,277 --> 00:50:02,475
There was this
really friendly brother over there…!

1624
00:50:02,476 --> 00:50:03,179
Oh, a brother!

1625
00:50:03,179 --> 00:50:04,678
My friend!

1626
00:50:04,679 --> 00:50:07,545
Hey yo!
Oh my god.

1627
00:50:07,778 --> 00:50:08,678
[Cheerfully greeting in Korean]
Hello!

1628
00:50:08,679 --> 00:50:11,078
- Hello. That's right, hello.
- Hello.

1629
00:50:11,445 --> 00:50:14,678
- He called me over, so I walked in, hypnotized.
- I already feel bad for him…

