1862
00:57:21,445 --> 00:57:22,978
Today… Ugh…

1863
00:57:23,145 --> 00:57:24,399
But this just looks so pathetic.

1864
00:57:24,400 --> 00:57:26,774
[Let’s stop meeting]
I don't want to see this black plastic bag anymore.

1865
00:57:26,775 --> 00:57:28,811
Yeah, the black plastic bag.

1866
00:57:29,146 --> 00:57:30,193
What? Is this water?

1867
00:57:30,194 --> 00:57:32,062
I thought it was kimbap.

1868
00:57:32,063 --> 00:57:33,611
- Wow.
- Just by the shape.

1869
00:57:35,146 --> 00:57:37,511
[Optimistic Pauper #1]
At least it’s a bit softer.

1870
00:57:37,512 --> 00:57:40,578
[Optimistic Pauper #2]
The one we had yesterday was a bit hard.

1871
00:57:40,579 --> 00:57:41,511
Water.

1872
00:57:41,711 --> 00:57:43,011
[Right in front of the princes' dining area]
They set the table right here.

1873
00:57:43,012 --> 00:57:44,678
My insides right now are really…

1874
00:57:45,178 --> 00:57:47,345
Sigh...

1875
00:57:47,346 --> 00:57:50,978
(From YOHAN’s POV)

1876
00:57:51,278 --> 00:57:53,911
[Tsk...]

1877
00:57:54,578 --> 00:57:56,778
[Feeling blue]
YOHAN, enjoy your meal...

1878
00:57:57,478 --> 00:57:59,445
[Trying to stay strong]
Enjoy your meal.

1879
00:57:59,945 --> 00:58:02,378
[Taking a chomp at the same time]

1880
00:58:02,379 --> 00:58:03,578
But, you know,

1881
00:58:03,579 --> 00:58:05,488
the more I eat this,
the more I get this flavor!

1882
00:58:05,489 --> 00:58:06,445
It's kind of like,

1883
00:58:06,446 --> 00:58:08,211
Pyeongyang Naengmyeon style!

1884
00:58:08,212 --> 00:58:10,478
- It's mild, but you keep going back for more.
- It's mild, but nice.

1885
00:58:10,911 --> 00:58:12,775
[While the paupers
are enjoying their own feast...]

1886
00:58:12,776 --> 00:58:14,245
Mmm!

1887
00:58:16,245 --> 00:58:17,475
Mmm!!

1888
00:58:17,476 --> 00:58:18,311
So good!

1889
00:58:18,378 --> 00:58:20,211
[The princes are
still living the peaceful life]

1890
00:58:20,578 --> 00:58:22,678
[No emotions]
I feel so bad for JISUNG, what do I do?

1891
00:58:23,211 --> 00:58:24,678
You should've switched with him.

1892
00:58:24,679 --> 00:58:26,778
But the rules say
we can't switch.

1893
00:58:27,111 --> 00:58:29,611
I can't just fix him a plate, right?

1894
00:58:29,612 --> 00:58:31,111
[What can we do…]
Oh.

1895
00:58:31,445 --> 00:58:32,778
[Slurp, slurp, slurp]

1896
00:58:34,081 --> 00:58:37,059
Maybe because I’m coming
from a pauper life, but I can't seem to eat well.

1897
00:58:37,060 --> 00:58:38,637
- Right?
- Yeah.

1898
00:58:39,245 --> 00:58:44,678
[When he does eat well,
just how much does he eat…?]

1899
00:58:44,978 --> 00:58:48,278
[Anyway, everyone's worried about the double pauper]
I can't really enjoy this. Our JISUNG, what do we do about him?

1900
00:58:48,688 --> 00:58:52,055
[Are you really worried though…?]
I just felt so bad for JISUNG.

1901
00:58:52,056 --> 00:58:54,573
But yesterday,
JISUNG was roasting you.

1902
00:58:54,574 --> 00:58:55,478
Oh, really?

1903
00:58:55,479 --> 00:58:57,645
You definitely told him…

1904
00:58:58,078 --> 00:59:00,378
When we were playing games,
LEETEUK whispered in my ear.

1905
00:59:00,379 --> 00:59:02,711
"JISUNG, you should be
the prince today."

1906
00:59:02,712 --> 00:59:04,378
[But only he became the prince]
But he actually worked really hard…

1907
00:59:04,379 --> 00:59:05,981
Hahahaha!

1908
00:59:05,982 --> 00:59:07,545
That just popped into my mind,
and it was so funny.

1909
00:59:07,546 --> 00:59:09,645
What a bad person!

1910
00:59:10,045 --> 00:59:12,645
[A bad person…]

1911
00:59:12,878 --> 00:59:15,011
Are we playing
the next game right away?

1912
00:59:15,111 --> 00:59:16,878
[Craving for a status upgrade]
I want to play games.

1913
00:59:17,911 --> 00:59:20,378
[Let's cheer up again]
Let's become more determined through this.

1914
00:59:21,011 --> 00:59:22,111
[Okay]

1915
00:59:22,112 --> 00:59:23,911
(Cheers)

1916
00:59:24,011 --> 00:59:26,078
[Bottom's up]

1917
00:59:26,888 --> 00:59:27,595
Huh?

1918
00:59:28,081 --> 00:59:28,675
Huh?

1919
00:59:29,911 --> 00:59:31,278
We don't vibe well…

1920
00:59:33,311 --> 00:59:34,678
Is this not it…?

1921
00:59:34,878 --> 00:59:36,178
[Even paupers can clink glasses]
Cheers! I said, "Cheers!"

1922
00:59:36,179 --> 00:59:37,145
Hahaha!

1923
00:59:37,146 --> 00:59:38,511
I did it like this…!

1924
00:59:38,512 --> 00:59:39,745
I didn't…
I didn't finish it yet.

1925
00:59:39,978 --> 00:59:42,811
[Wishing to escape the pauper life]
Adios!

1926
00:59:42,812 --> 00:59:46,178
[He’s a pauper too]
I really hope JISUNG becomes a prince.

1927
00:59:46,378 --> 00:59:48,611
[Choking up]
I don’t know.

1928
00:59:48,778 --> 00:59:49,978
(Pauper JISUNG)
I thought,

1929
00:59:49,979 --> 00:59:52,378
"No matter what,
I will become the prince."

1930
00:59:52,379 --> 00:59:55,678
[I have to be the prince…]
First, I have to become a prince.

1931
00:59:57,778 --> 01:00:00,711
["ALL or NOTHING"
Day 2 status resets]

1932
01:00:04,272 --> 01:00:05,454
Wow, that’s cool.

1933
01:00:05,455 --> 01:00:06,967
So cool!
This is really cool!

1934
01:00:07,558 --> 01:00:08,398
It's really huge!

1935
01:00:10,179 --> 01:00:13,045
- Wow, look over there! So cool!
- Wow!

1936
01:00:13,588 --> 01:00:15,812
This can’t be real.

1937
01:00:16,367 --> 01:00:19,678
[Totally overwhelmed]
I wondered what they did here.

1938
01:00:19,911 --> 01:00:24,178
[Luxor Temple]

1939
01:00:24,179 --> 01:00:27,811
[Where Pharaoh’s time stands still]

1940
01:00:34,245 --> 01:00:38,511
[A sanctuary infused with the power
of Pharaohs and the breath of gods]

1941
01:00:38,512 --> 01:00:42,945
[With ancient records carved
deep into stone walls]

1942
01:00:42,946 --> 01:00:47,345
[a sacred space shaped
by colossal stone pillars]

1943
01:00:47,645 --> 01:00:51,545
[and endless rows of
countless sphinxes]

1944
01:00:51,711 --> 01:00:52,778
[Luxor Temple]

1945
01:00:52,785 --> 01:00:54,845
[Built by Amenhotep III
and expanded by Ramses II]

1946
01:00:54,846 --> 01:00:56,651
[An icon of ancient Egyptian
civilization that’s endured 3,400 years]

1947
01:00:57,011 --> 01:00:59,711
[Staff] The very spot
you’re standing on now

1948
01:00:59,712 --> 01:01:02,445
is an ancient temple
on the east side of the Nile River.

1949
01:01:02,446 --> 01:01:03,378
This is the Luxor Temple.

1950
01:01:03,379 --> 01:01:04,578
- Wow!
- Luxor!

1951
01:01:04,579 --> 01:01:06,545
Oh, so it's Luxor Temple!

1952
01:01:06,711 --> 01:01:10,378
If you look in the back,
you can see the tall pillar on the left,

1953
01:01:10,379 --> 01:01:10,978
- Yes.
- Yes.

1954
01:01:10,979 --> 01:01:14,144
- That's called an obelisk.
- An obelisk.

1955
01:01:14,278 --> 01:01:16,678
[Obelisk, a symbol
glorifying the power of the sun god]

1956
01:01:17,978 --> 01:01:21,778
[But where’s the pillar on the right?]

1957
01:01:21,779 --> 01:01:23,911
[Staff] Do you know
where the right pillar is?

1958
01:01:23,912 --> 01:01:25,478
Was it in France?

1959
01:01:25,479 --> 01:01:27,245
[So close to the answer]
Oh, should we narrow it down a bit more?

1960
01:01:27,246 --> 01:01:28,181
- Paris?
- Paris.

1961
01:01:28,182 --> 01:01:29,112
[Almost there...!]
Okay, just a little more.

1962
01:01:29,112 --> 01:01:30,378
The Louvre?

1963
01:01:30,379 --> 01:01:32,068
[Staff] The obelisk is
at the Place de la Concorde in Paris.

1964
01:01:32,069 --> 01:01:33,845
Oh, yes, that's right

1965
01:01:34,111 --> 01:01:35,278
[The Obelisk
at the Place de la Concorde]

1966
01:01:35,285 --> 01:01:37,671
[Muhammad Ali,
the then-Governor of Egypt,]

1967
01:01:37,672 --> 01:01:40,051
[gifted it to France
to strengthen their friendship]

1968
01:01:40,456 --> 01:01:41,676
Wow, that's so cool.

1969
01:01:42,178 --> 01:01:44,545
[Staff] As you probably saw earlier,

1970
01:01:44,546 --> 01:01:45,745
this place actually

1971
01:01:45,746 --> 01:01:48,161
closes at 8 PM.

1972
01:01:48,162 --> 01:01:49,445
Oh!

1973
01:01:49,446 --> 01:01:50,778
So we rented it
after closing time?

1974
01:01:50,779 --> 01:01:52,378
Yes, just for you guys,

1975
01:01:52,379 --> 01:01:53,878
(Thank you!)
they rented it out for us.

1976
01:01:53,879 --> 01:01:55,511
- That's amazing! Wow!
- Wow!

1977
01:01:55,512 --> 01:01:57,945
[Staff] Before we dive
into the real mission,

1978
01:01:57,946 --> 01:01:59,678
we'll give you 20 minutes

1979
01:01:59,679 --> 01:02:01,111
to freely explore
on your own and come back.

1980
01:02:01,112 --> 01:02:02,080
…to freely explore
on your own and come back.

1981
01:02:02,081 --> 01:02:03,777
- Oh…
- Oh, this is…

1982
01:02:03,778 --> 01:02:06,078
[Why the sightseeing?]
Oh, this is iffy. It's very iffy.

1983
01:02:06,079 --> 01:02:08,078
[Overly suspicious humans]
Is this another memory test?

1984
01:02:08,079 --> 01:02:10,345
[Strategist SHINDONG activates]
I'd better snap some pics then.

1985
01:02:10,346 --> 01:02:12,578
[It's seriously
for them to sightsee…]

1986
01:02:12,579 --> 01:02:16,145
[Already memorizing the whole temple]
There's a ton of bird images.

1987
01:02:16,811 --> 01:02:18,578
[First, take the shots]

1988
01:02:19,545 --> 01:02:21,545
[And then…]

1989
01:02:21,546 --> 01:02:23,478
[Someone misunderstood it as first-come, first-served]
Oh, you're taking the hard path.

1990
01:02:23,479 --> 01:02:24,678
No…!

1991
01:02:26,111 --> 01:02:28,111
[Pauper JISUNG heads out too]

1992
01:02:28,511 --> 01:02:29,778
[Everyone takes off quickly]

1993
01:02:29,779 --> 01:02:31,178
There’s no time to waste!

1994
01:02:31,179 --> 01:02:33,445
Once you start doubting everything,
you start doing worse.

1995
01:02:33,446 --> 01:02:35,278
[Except one person]
You just gotta enjoy it!

1996
01:02:35,279 --> 01:02:37,378
These guys are way
too greedy, seriously.

1997
01:02:37,379 --> 01:02:39,145
[Just a lazy person]

1998
01:02:39,345 --> 01:02:41,045
(Passing by)
Wow, they're real stones!

1999
01:02:41,046 --> 01:02:42,711
[Busy, so busy]
This is no joke.

2000
01:02:43,578 --> 01:02:47,645
You have to take it easy.
You can't think something's gonna happen.

2001
01:02:50,878 --> 01:02:54,345
[Thoroughly counting the pillars]

2002
01:02:56,245 --> 01:02:58,145
[Chronically suspicious]
I can’t trust the production team at all,

2003
01:02:58,146 --> 01:03:01,578
so I was trying to memorize
the number of pillars the temple had.

2004
01:03:01,579 --> 01:03:03,345
[Starting to doubt everything]
I feel like it'll be a question.

2005
01:03:03,645 --> 01:03:07,245
I took pictures
and counted every pillar.

2006
01:03:07,571 --> 01:03:10,178
[The scariest person...]
I looked at everything in detail.

2007
01:03:10,179 --> 01:03:13,378
Just relax and enjoy it!

2008
01:03:15,278 --> 01:03:17,108
- You seem to be trying harder than anyone else.
- No, no.

2009
01:03:17,109 --> 01:03:18,278
I mean, well…

2010
01:03:18,279 --> 01:03:20,478
I'm just here to have fun.

2011
01:03:21,678 --> 01:03:22,778
[Found a guide map]

2012
01:03:22,779 --> 01:03:24,479
Wow!

2013
01:03:24,480 --> 01:03:25,378
Can I not use flash?

2014
01:03:27,074 --> 01:03:29,645
[Sensing something and approaching]
Oh, yeah, this is important.

2015
01:03:29,779 --> 01:03:30,578
This is important?

2016
01:03:31,162 --> 01:03:32,978
Doesn't it look like
it'd be important?

2017
01:03:33,178 --> 01:03:36,345
[Suddenly, everyone gathers around the map]
Yeah.

2018
01:03:37,352 --> 01:03:39,472
(What are they looking at...?)
Everyone left this behind…

2019
01:03:39,473 --> 01:03:41,483
YOHAN, you're blocking it!

2020
01:03:43,011 --> 01:03:44,471
(Curious)
What is this?

2021
01:03:44,472 --> 01:03:45,770
I also took pictures,
just in case.

2022
01:03:45,771 --> 01:03:47,278
You never know,
so better safe than sorry.

2023
01:03:47,279 --> 01:03:49,145
(Checked what it was)
Oh, JOHNNY blocked it…

2024
01:03:49,146 --> 01:03:51,178
[After pretending not to care,]
Oh, wait. It shook! Oh, okay.

2025
01:03:51,179 --> 01:03:53,281
[he snaps a shot while spewing nonsense]
Hey, but if you take a picture, do you get anything from it?

2026
01:03:53,282 --> 01:03:55,490
So, like…!
For me, it's just…No.

2027
01:03:56,878 --> 01:04:01,845
But LEETEUK, you said we should enjoy it,
but you're taking pictures.

2028
01:04:01,846 --> 01:04:04,611
[What are you talking about? I am enjoying it]
Hey, I’m having fun in my own way right now.

2029
01:04:06,445 --> 01:04:07,645
They must be a married couple.

2030
01:04:07,778 --> 01:04:11,445
[Wedding MC expert]
You two are a perfect match!

2031
01:04:13,111 --> 01:04:15,211
LEETEUK's filming
a variety show again.

2032
01:04:15,278 --> 01:04:17,478
Oh, right! I'm filming too.

2033
01:04:19,075 --> 01:04:20,975
This all feels kinda unreal.

2034
01:04:21,101 --> 01:04:23,577
[Spotting something?]
Whoa, what’s that over there?

2035
01:04:24,963 --> 01:04:25,863
Wow!

2036
01:04:28,378 --> 01:04:31,345
Wow! Wow!!

2037
01:04:31,346 --> 01:04:32,549
This place is seriously cool!

2038
01:04:32,550 --> 01:04:33,475
This place is amazing.

2039
01:04:33,745 --> 01:04:37,197
[A vast plaza surrounded
by dozens of towering pillars]

2040
01:04:37,198 --> 01:04:38,677
Wow, there are
so many pillars here.

2041
01:04:40,089 --> 01:04:42,996
[A sight too amazing for just your eyes]
Wow, this is incredible.

2042
01:04:42,997 --> 01:04:44,745
Wow!

2043
01:04:46,578 --> 01:04:49,278
They must have held
festivals of some sort here, right?

2044
01:04:49,279 --> 01:04:50,498
This place is seriously stunning.

2045
01:04:51,296 --> 01:04:52,289
Wow!

2046
01:04:53,677 --> 01:04:54,570
Oh, oh!

2047
01:04:58,375 --> 01:05:00,678
Like, there aren't a lot of people

2048
01:05:00,679 --> 01:05:03,381
who can see this place
empty, like us, right?

2049
01:05:03,382 --> 01:05:04,078
That's right.

2050
01:05:04,079 --> 01:05:06,911
[A sense of freedom
in the vast, open space]

2051
01:05:07,845 --> 01:05:10,011
[JOHNNY] For this trip,

2052
01:05:10,012 --> 01:05:13,111
it was one of
the most memorable moments.

2053
01:05:13,978 --> 01:05:17,578
When we went from Cairo to Luxor,

2054
01:05:17,579 --> 01:05:20,878
[The Luxor Temple he saw in the car]
I saw the Luxor Temple, because it was massive!

2055
01:05:20,879 --> 01:05:23,345
I said I really wanted
to visit that place later.

2056
01:05:23,611 --> 01:05:27,578
[He finally sees it in person]
I went, and it was that place!

2057
01:05:28,311 --> 01:05:31,478
I was so, so excited.

2058
01:05:32,445 --> 01:05:34,278
[Moving deeper into the temple]
Wow, look at the murals on the walls.

2059
01:05:34,279 --> 01:05:35,864
There are so many murals!

2060
01:05:35,865 --> 01:05:37,478
Every single wall
is covered in drawings!

2061
01:05:38,611 --> 01:05:39,595
[Ancient records fill every surface]

2062
01:05:39,596 --> 01:05:42,178
There isn’t
a single blank spot anywhere.

2063
01:05:42,611 --> 01:05:44,278
[A heritage thousands of years old]

2064
01:05:44,279 --> 01:05:45,391
They're all covered in drawings.

2065
01:05:45,392 --> 01:05:46,278
[and the moment you face it
thousands of years later]

2066
01:05:46,279 --> 01:05:48,911
These are
the actual murals, right?

2067
01:05:49,271 --> 01:05:51,670
If you look closely,
they're all different drawings.

2068
01:05:51,671 --> 01:05:52,778
Oh, really?

2069
01:05:52,978 --> 01:05:54,378
The types of food are different.

2070
01:05:54,379 --> 01:05:55,711
This one’s veggies.

2071
01:05:56,045 --> 01:05:57,872
[The lives and thoughts passed down to us]
This is something else.

2072
01:05:57,873 --> 01:06:00,311
[from ancient humanity]
Every dish is unique

2073
01:06:01,078 --> 01:06:03,611
[SHINDONG] It's not about
it being good or bad.

2074
01:06:03,612 --> 01:06:05,745
It just didn't feel real.

2075
01:06:07,825 --> 01:06:10,278
[As you walk, enchanted by the grandeur,
a path that appears like a miracle]

2076
01:06:10,279 --> 01:06:12,677
- Leaving behind the grand sightseeing.
- Yes.

2077
01:06:12,678 --> 01:06:16,578
[Staff] It’s time to
decide your status with a game.

2078
01:06:16,579 --> 01:06:17,478
Please!

2079
01:06:17,745 --> 01:06:19,845
There was a reason
they told us to wear sneakers.

2080
01:06:20,178 --> 01:06:23,378
[This place we’re at is called "The Avenue of Sphinxes"]
This is a place known as the Avenue of Sphinxes.

2081
01:06:23,379 --> 01:06:24,411
So they were all sphinxes.

2082
01:06:24,412 --> 01:06:26,911
[Staff] You all saw
the countless number of sphinxes here, right?

2083
01:06:26,912 --> 01:06:27,578
Yes.

2084
01:06:27,978 --> 01:06:30,378
[The Avenue of Sphinxes]
This is the Luxor Temple,

2085
01:06:30,379 --> 01:06:32,345
[From Luxor Temple to Karnak Temple in the north]
And there’s a place called Karnak Temple.

2086
01:06:32,346 --> 01:06:33,678
[there are countless sphinxes]
These sphinxes

2087
01:06:33,679 --> 01:06:35,164
[lined up for about 2.7 km]
supposedly connect all the way there.

2088
01:06:35,165 --> 01:06:37,678
[At the Opet Festival,
during the annual Nile flood season,]

2089
01:06:37,679 --> 01:06:40,311
[It was used as the Pharaoh’s parade route]
This is the path that was used for festival processions.

2090
01:06:40,312 --> 01:06:42,545
[The immortal Sphinx
shines brilliantly in the dark]

2091
01:06:42,546 --> 01:06:45,112
[WANGGEOZ, Assalamu Alaykum]

2092
01:06:45,445 --> 01:06:47,745
[Staff] When you think of
the Sphinx, what comes to mind?

2093
01:06:47,746 --> 01:06:48,678
A quiz.

2094
01:06:48,679 --> 01:06:49,578
That's right.

2095
01:06:49,778 --> 01:06:51,201
Starting right now in this place,

2096
01:06:51,681 --> 01:06:53,581
[The "Sphinx's Riddle" mission]
The Sphinx's Riddle!

2097
01:06:53,582 --> 01:06:54,444
Oh!

2098
01:06:54,445 --> 01:06:56,211
